window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b100-452fb5b5bd5380dd.json"]={sha256:"452fb5b5bd5380dd7384f5ffc4125f4fe0ade8561bba484747687189cf1cbe8f",value:{"id":"b100","title":"建築模組化吊裝與接合","titleEn":"Volumetric modular-building lifting and connections","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從體積模組的角柱荷載路徑與雙層樓板出發，說明模組間繫結與防連續倒塌、角部接頭與螺栓接合、吊點與吊裝框，再處理起重機選型與風速限制、堆疊公差與墊片、工廠出廠檢驗、現場接頭與防火防水檢查，最後談模組間空腔的耐久與模組履歷交接，並以新加坡 The Clement Canopy、紐約 461 Dean Street 與蒙特婁 Habitat 67 對照。","summaryEn":"Starting from corner-post load paths and double floors in volumetric modules, explain inter-module ties and progressive-collapse resistance, corner joints and bolting, lift points and lifting frames, then crane selection and wind limits, stacking tolerances and shims, factory release inspection, site joint, fire-stopping and waterproofing checks, and finally durability of inter-module cavities and module-record handover, compared with The Clement Canopy in Singapore, 461 Dean Street in New York and Habitat 67 in Montreal.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-facade-digital","subcategoryTitle":"帷幕牆、垂直運輸與數位營建","subcategoryTitleEn":"Facades, vertical transport and digital construction","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-facade-digital","learningTags":["structures","st-facade-digital","modular"],"architectureFamily":"modular","architectureNodes":[["工廠製造與品管","Factory fabrication and QA"],["運輸與吊裝","Transport and lifting"],["角部接頭與繫結","Corner joints and ties"],["核心筒與抗側力系統","Core and lateral system"],["防水、防火與空腔","Waterproofing, fire stopping and cavities"],["模組履歷與交接","Module records and handover"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[2,4],[0,5],[4,5]],"diagram":{"type":"modular","labels":["工廠製造與品管","運輸與吊裝","角部接頭與繫結","核心筒與抗側力系統","防水、防火與空腔"],"labelsEn":["Factory fabrication and QA","Transport and lifting","Corner joints and ties","Core and lateral system","Waterproofing, fire stopping and cavities"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：一棟 20 層鋼構模組建築，每層 8 個模組，共 8×20 = 160 個。每個模組吊裝循環（掛鉤、吊升、定位、鎖固、回程）40 分鐘，總吊裝時間 160×40/60 ≈ 106.7 小時；每天可吊裝 6 小時，需 106.7/6 ≈ 17.8 天，若預留 25% 風雨停工，約 17.8/0.75 ≈ 23.7 天，取 24 個工作天。起重機在 40 m 半徑的額定荷重 28 t，模組 22 t 加吊裝框 2.5 t 與索具 0.5 t，吊重 25 t，使用率 25/28 ≈ 89%。若裝修與設備使模組增重 8% 成 22×1.08 = 23.76 t，吊重 26.76 t，使用率 26.76/28 ≈ 96%，超過 90% 的規劃上限，須縮短半徑、移位起重機或改用較大機型。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際專案；實際吊裝計畫須由合格的吊掛負責人核准。","textEn":"Design exercise: a 20-storey steel modular building has 8 modules per floor, 8×20 = 160 in all. Each lifting cycle (hook on, hoist, place, bolt, return) takes 40 minutes, so total hook time is 160×40/60 ≈ 106.7 hours; at 6 lifting hours a day this needs 106.7/6 ≈ 17.8 days, and allowing 25% for wind and rain about 17.8/0.75 ≈ 23.7 days, so 24 working days. The crane is rated 28 t at 40 m radius; a 22 t module plus a 2.5 t lifting frame and 0.5 t of rigging gives a 25 t hook load and 25/28 ≈ 89% utilisation. If finishes and equipment add 8% to the module, 22×1.08 = 23.76 t, the hook load is 26.76 t and utilisation 26.76/28 ≈ 96%, above a 90% planning limit, so the radius must be shortened, the crane moved or a larger crane used. Values are teaching assumptions, not any real project; an actual lifting plan must be approved by a competent lifting supervisor.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b100-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「體積模組的荷載路徑與結構系統」與「側向力傳遞、整體性與防連續倒塌」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Load paths and structural systems of volumetric modules\" and \"Lateral load transfer, robustness and progressive collapse\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b100-v13-01","title":"體積模組的荷載路徑與結構系統：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Load paths and structural systems of volumetric modules: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「角柱與雙層樓板」如何影響建築模組化吊裝與接合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Corner posts and double floors” governs force, deformation or durability in “Volumetric modular-building lifting and connections”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"體積模組是在工廠完成結構、隔間、機電與裝修的立體箱體，到工地後像積木一樣堆疊。鋼構模組通常以四角的方管柱與上下框梁承受重力，荷載沿角柱一路往下傳；新加坡 PPVC 一類的混凝土模組則以六面混凝土板承重。每個模組都有自己的地板與天花板，形成雙層樓板與雙層牆，自重與樓高都比傳統構造大；較高的模組建築通常另以現澆混凝土核心筒或斜撐承受側力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「角柱與雙層樓板」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A volumetric module is a three-dimensional box whose structure, partitions, services and finishes are completed in a factory and then stacked on site like building blocks. Steel modules usually carry gravity through square hollow-section posts at the four corners and top and bottom edge beams, so load runs down the corner posts; concrete modules such as Singapore's PPVC carry it through six-sided concrete panels. Every module has its own floor and ceiling, giving double floors and walls that add weight and storey height compared with conventional construction, and taller modular buildings usually resist lateral load with a cast-in-place concrete core or bracing. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Corner posts and double floors” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：模組 3.6 m × 12 m = 43.2 m²，靜載 4.0 kPa（雙層樓板與天花）、活載 2.0 kPa，設計荷重 1.2×4.0 + 1.6×2.0 = 8.0 kPa，每模組每層 43.2×8.0 = 345.6 kN，由 4 根角柱各分擔 86.4 kN；上方 10 層累積 864 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 3.6 m × 12 m module covers 43.2 m²; with 4.0 kPa dead load (double floor and ceiling) and 2.0 kPa live load the design load is 1.2×4.0 + 1.6×2.0 = 8.0 kPa, so each module carries 43.2×8.0 = 345.6 kN per storey, 86.4 kN on each of four corner posts; ten storeys above accumulate 864 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「模組在工廠已經做好結構，堆疊後不需要整體結構分析。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Since each module's structure is finished in the factory, the stacked building needs no overall structural analysis.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「角柱與雙層樓板」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Corner posts and double floors”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-01-k1","title":"體積模組的荷載路徑與結構系統","titleEn":"Load paths and structural systems of volumetric modules","text":"體積模組是在工廠完成結構、隔間、機電與裝修的立體箱體，到工地後像積木一樣堆疊。鋼構模組通常以四角的方管柱與上下框梁承受重力，荷載沿角柱一路往下傳；新加坡 PPVC 一類的混凝土模組則以六面混凝土板承重。","textEn":"A volumetric module is a three-dimensional box whose structure, partitions, services and finishes are completed in a factory and then stacked on site like building blocks. Steel modules usually carry gravity through square hollow-section posts at the four corners and top and bottom edge beams, so load runs down the corner posts; concrete modules such as Singapore's PPVC carry it through six-sided concrete panels.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模組在工廠已經做好結構，堆疊後不需要整體結構分析。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Since each module's structure is finished in the factory, the stacked building needs no overall structural analysis. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「體積模組的荷載路徑與結構系統」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Load paths and structural systems of volumetric modules\" is correct?","options":["模組在工廠已經做好結構，堆疊後不需要整體結構分析。","體積模組是在工廠完成結構、隔間、機電與裝修的立體箱體，到工地後像積木一樣堆疊。","模組只要上下疊好，自重就足以讓建築維持整體性。"],"optionsEn":["Since each module's structure is finished in the factory, the stacked building needs no overall structural analysis.","A volumetric module is a three-dimensional box whose structure, partitions, services and finishes are completed in a factory and then stacked on site like building blocks.","As long as modules are stacked properly, self-weight alone keeps the building intact."],"answer":1,"explanation":"體積模組是在工廠完成結構、隔間、機電與裝修的立體箱體，到工地後像積木一樣堆疊。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A volumetric module is a three-dimensional box whose structure, partitions, services and finishes are completed in a factory and then stacked on site like building blocks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b100-v13-02","title":"體積模組的荷載路徑與結構系統：定量估算","titleEn":"Load paths and structural systems of volumetric modules: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「角柱與雙層樓板」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Corner posts and double floors” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：模組 3.6 m × 12 m = 43.2 m²，靜載 4.0 kPa（雙層樓板與天花）、活載 2.0 kPa，設計荷重 1.2×4.0 + 1.6×2.0 = 8.0 kPa，每模組每層 43.2×8.0 = 345.6 kN，由 4 根角柱各分擔 86.4 kN；上方 10 層累積 864 kN。角柱採 200×200×10 mm 方管（面積約 7,600 mm²），軸應力約 864,000/7,600 ≈ 114 MPa。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 3.6 m × 12 m module covers 43.2 m²; with 4.0 kPa dead load (double floor and ceiling) and 2.0 kPa live load the design load is 1.2×4.0 + 1.6×2.0 = 8.0 kPa, so each module carries 43.2×8.0 = 345.6 kN per storey, 86.4 kN on each of four corner posts; ten storeys above accumulate 864 kN. A 200×200×10 mm SHS post (area about 7,600 mm²) then sees about 864,000/7,600 ≈ 114 MPa axial stress. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：結構分析要以實際的角柱、框梁與接頭勁度建立堆疊模型，檢查角柱軸力、局部壓屈與接頭承壓；並核對模組之間是否真如假設只在角部傳力（例如墊塊或承壓板位置），工廠以抽樣試驗確認方管與焊接品質。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The structural analysis should model the stack with the actual stiffness of corner posts, edge beams and joints, checking post axial force, local buckling and joint bearing, and confirm that modules really bear on each other only at the corners as assumed (for example at packers or bearing plates); the factory confirms hollow-section and weld quality by sample testing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"模組 3.6 m × 12 m = 43.2 m²，靜載 4.0 kPa（雙層樓板與天花）、活載 2.0 kPa，設計荷重 1.2×4.0 + 1.6×2.0 = 8.0 kPa，每模組每層 43.2×8.0 = 345.6 kN，由 4 根角柱各分擔 86.4 kN；上方 10 層累積 864 kN。角柱採 200×200×10 mm 方管（面積約 7,600 mm²），軸應力約 864,000/7,600 ≈ 114 MPa。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A 3.6 m × 12 m module covers 43.2 m²; with 4.0 kPa dead load (double floor and ceiling) and 2.0 kPa live load the design load is 1.2×4.0 + 1.6×2.0 = 8.0 kPa, so each module carries 43.2×8.0 = 345.6 kN per storey, 86.4 kN on each of four corner posts; ten storeys above accumulate 864 kN. A 200×200×10 mm SHS post (area about 7,600 mm²) then sees about 864,000/7,600 ≈ 114 MPa axial stress. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「體積模組的荷載路徑與結構系統」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Load paths and structural systems of volumetric modules\", which statement holds?","options":["模組既然能承受使用荷載，用任何方式吊起來都不會受損。","只要每個模組都在製造公差內，堆疊後整棟建築也必然在公差內。","模組 3.6 m × 12 m = 43.2 m²，靜載 4.0 kPa（雙層樓板與天花）、活載 2.0 kPa，設計荷重 1.2×4.0 + 1.6×2.0 = 8.0 kPa，每模組每層 43.2×8.0 = 345.6 kN，由 4 根角柱各分擔 86.4 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Since a module can carry service loads, any way of lifting it will do no harm.","If every module is within its fabrication tolerance, the stacked building must be too.","A 3.6 m × 12 m module covers 43.2 m²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模組 3.6 m × 12 m = 43.2 m²，靜載 4.0 kPa（雙層樓板與天花）、活載 2.0 kPa，設計荷重 1.2×4.0 + 1.6×2.0 = 8.0 kPa，每模組每層 43.2×8.0 = 345.6 kN，由 4 根角柱各分擔 86.4 kN；上方 10 層累積 864 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 3.6 m × 12 m module covers 43.2 m²; with 4.0 kPa dead load (double floor and ceiling) and 2.0 kPa live load the design load is 1.2×4.0 + 1.6×2.0 = 8.0 kPa, so each module carries 43.2×8.0 = 345.6 kN per storey, 86.4 kN on each of four corner posts; ten storeys above accumulate 864 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b100-v13-03","title":"體積模組的荷載路徑與結構系統：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Load paths and structural systems of volumetric modules: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「角柱與雙層樓板」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Corner posts and double floors” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"結構分析要以實際的角柱、框梁與接頭勁度建立堆疊模型，檢查角柱軸力、局部壓屈與接頭承壓；並核對模組之間是否真如假設只在角部傳力（例如墊塊或承壓板位置），工廠以抽樣試驗確認方管與焊接品質。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The structural analysis should model the stack with the actual stiffness of corner posts, edge beams and joints, checking post axial force, local buckling and joint bearing, and confirm that modules really bear on each other only at the corners as assumed (for example at packers or bearing plates); the factory confirms hollow-section and weld quality by sample testing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：結構設計者要在圖上標明每一處模組間的承壓點、墊塊材料與厚度，並把「非承壓區保持間隙」列為安裝檢查項目；超過一定層數的模組建築須設計獨立的抗側力系統並經結構審查。","observationEn":"Site practice: The structural designer must mark every inter-module bearing point, packer material and thickness on the drawings and make ‘keep non-bearing zones clear’ an installation check item; modular buildings above a set height need an independent lateral system, designed and passed through structural review.","failure":"注意干擾：若模組間在樓板邊緣意外接觸而非只在角部承壓，荷載會流入未設計承壓的框梁，造成局部變形與裝修開裂；角柱接頭偏心產生附加彎矩，可能使高層堆疊下方的角柱提早壓屈。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If modules accidentally bear along floor edges rather than only at the corners, load flows into edge beams not designed for bearing, causing local distortion and cracked finishes; eccentric corner joints add bending that can buckle lower corner posts early in a tall stack. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"結構分析要以實際的角柱、框梁與接頭勁度建立堆疊模型，檢查角柱軸力、局部壓屈與接頭承壓；並核對模組之間是否真如假設只在角部傳力（例如墊塊或承壓板位置），工廠以抽樣試驗確認方管與焊接品質。","textEn":"The structural analysis should model the stack with the actual stiffness of corner posts, edge beams and joints, checking post axial force, local buckling and joint bearing, and confirm that modules really bear on each other only at the corners as assumed (for example at packers or bearing plates); the factory confirms hollow-section and weld quality by sample testing.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"結構設計者要在圖上標明每一處模組間的承壓點、墊塊材料與厚度，並把「非承壓區保持間隙」列為安裝檢查項目；超過一定層數的模組建築須設計獨立的抗側力系統並經結構審查。","textEn":"The structural designer must mark every inter-module bearing point, packer material and thickness on the drawings and make ‘keep non-bearing zones clear’ an installation check item; modular buildings above a set height need an independent lateral system, designed and passed through structural review.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「體積模組的荷載路徑與結構系統」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Load paths and structural systems of volumetric modules\"?","options":["結構分析要以實際的角柱、框梁與接頭勁度建立堆疊模型，檢查角柱軸力、局部壓屈與接頭承壓。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","扳手鎖到規定扭矩，就代表螺栓預拉力一定正確。"],"optionsEn":["The structural analysis should model the stack with the actual stiffness of corner posts, edge beams and joints, checking post axial force, local buckling and joint bearing, and confirm that modules really bear on each other only at the corners as assumed (for example at packers or bearing plates).","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Tightening to the specified torque guarantees the correct bolt preload."],"answer":0,"explanation":"結構分析要以實際的角柱、框梁與接頭勁度建立堆疊模型，檢查角柱軸力、局部壓屈與接頭承壓；並核對模組之間是否真如假設只在角部傳力（例如墊塊或承壓板位置），工廠以抽樣試驗確認方管與焊接品質。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The structural analysis should model the stack with the actual stiffness of corner posts, edge beams and joints, checking post axial force, local buckling and joint bearing, and confirm that modules really bear on each other only at the corners as assumed (for example at packers or bearing plates); the factory confirms hollow-section and weld quality by sample testing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b100-v13-04","title":"體積模組的荷載路徑與結構系統：失效診斷","titleEn":"Load paths and structural systems of volumetric modules: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「角柱與雙層樓板」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Corner posts and double floors” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若模組間在樓板邊緣意外接觸而非只在角部承壓，荷載會流入未設計承壓的框梁，造成局部變形與裝修開裂；角柱接頭偏心產生附加彎矩，可能使高層堆疊下方的角柱提早壓屈。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If modules accidentally bear along floor edges rather than only at the corners, load flows into edge beams not designed for bearing, causing local distortion and cracked finishes; eccentric corner joints add bending that can buckle lower corner posts early in a tall stack. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：每個模組都有自己的地板與天花板，形成雙層樓板與雙層牆，自重與樓高都比傳統構造大；較高的模組建築通常另以現澆混凝土核心筒或斜撐承受側力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Every module has its own floor and ceiling, giving double floors and walls that add weight and storey height compared with conventional construction, and taller modular buildings usually resist lateral load with a cast-in-place concrete core or bracing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模組在工廠已經做好結構，堆疊後不需要整體結構分析。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Since each module's structure is finished in the factory, the stacked building needs no overall structural analysis.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若模組間在樓板邊緣意外接觸而非只在角部承壓，荷載會流入未設計承壓的框梁，造成局部變形與裝修開裂；角柱接頭偏心產生附加彎矩，可能使高層堆疊下方的角柱提早壓屈。","textEn":"If modules accidentally bear along floor edges rather than only at the corners, load flows into edge beams not designed for bearing, causing local distortion and cracked finishes; eccentric corner joints add bending that can buckle lower corner posts early in a tall stack.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「體積模組的荷載路徑與結構系統」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Load paths and structural systems of volumetric modules\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若模組間在樓板邊緣意外接觸而非只在角部承壓，荷載會流入未設計承壓的框梁，造成局部變形與裝修開裂；角柱接頭偏心產生附加彎矩，可能使高層堆疊下方的角柱提早壓屈。","模組只要上下疊好，自重就足以讓建築維持整體性。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","If modules accidentally bear along floor edges rather than only at the corners, load flows into edge beams not designed for bearing, causing local distortion and cracked finishes.","As long as modules are stacked properly, self-weight alone keeps the building intact."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若模組間在樓板邊緣意外接觸而非只在角部承壓，荷載會流入未設計承壓的框梁，造成局部變形與裝修開裂；角柱接頭偏心產生附加彎矩，可能使高層堆疊下方的角柱提早壓屈。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If modules accidentally bear along floor edges rather than only at the corners, load flows into edge beams not designed for bearing, causing local distortion and cracked finishes; eccentric corner joints add bending that can buckle lower corner posts early in a tall stack. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b100-v13-05","title":"側向力傳遞、整體性與防連續倒塌：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Lateral load transfer, robustness and progressive collapse: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「模組間水平繫結」如何影響建築模組化吊裝與接合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Inter-module horizontal ties” governs force, deformation or durability in “Volumetric modular-building lifting and connections”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"側向風力與地震力先由每個模組的樓板與天花板收集，再透過模組間的水平連接板傳到核心筒或斜撐模組。模組之間只靠少數點連接，若連接設計不足，建築在偶發事件中缺乏整體性，一個模組受損就可能讓相鄰模組失去支承。因此設計要提供水平與垂直繫結，並檢核移除一個模組或一根角柱後，上方荷載能否由懸臂作用或繫結重新分配，這是模組建築防止連續倒塌的核心。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「模組間水平繫結」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wind and seismic forces are first collected by each module's floor and ceiling, then passed through horizontal inter-module plates to the core or braced modules. Modules are joined at only a few points, so weak connections leave the building without integrity in an accident, and damage to one module can strip support from its neighbours. The design must therefore provide horizontal and vertical ties and check whether, with one module or corner post removed, the load above can be redistributed by cantilever action or ties; this is the core of preventing progressive collapse in modular buildings. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Inter-module horizontal ties” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：參考 EN 1991-1-7 附錄 A 的內部繫結型式 T = 0.8(g_k + ψq_k)·s·L，且不小於 75 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Following the internal-tie form of EN 1991-1-7 Annex A, T = 0.8(g_k + ψq_k)·s·L but not less than 75 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「模組只要上下疊好，自重就足以讓建築維持整體性。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"As long as modules are stacked properly, self-weight alone keeps the building intact.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「模組間水平繫結」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Inter-module horizontal ties”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-05-k1","title":"側向力傳遞、整體性與防連續倒塌","titleEn":"Lateral load transfer, robustness and progressive collapse","text":"側向風力與地震力先由每個模組的樓板與天花板收集，再透過模組間的水平連接板傳到核心筒或斜撐模組。模組之間只靠少數點連接，若連接設計不足，建築在偶發事件中缺乏整體性，一個模組受損就可能讓相鄰模組失去支承。","textEn":"Wind and seismic forces are first collected by each module's floor and ceiling, then passed through horizontal inter-module plates to the core or braced modules. Modules are joined at only a few points, so weak connections leave the building without integrity in an accident, and damage to one module can strip support from its neighbours.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模組只要上下疊好，自重就足以讓建築維持整體性。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: As long as modules are stacked properly, self-weight alone keeps the building intact. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「側向力傳遞、整體性與防連續倒塌」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lateral load transfer, robustness and progressive collapse\" is correct?","options":["模組只要上下疊好，自重就足以讓建築維持整體性。","模組接頭只要強度計算通過，安裝方式可以留給現場決定。","側向風力與地震力先由每個模組的樓板與天花板收集，再透過模組間的水平連接板傳到核心筒或斜撐模組。"],"optionsEn":["As long as modules are stacked properly, self-weight alone keeps the building intact.","Once a module joint passes the strength calculation, how it is installed can be left to the site.","Wind and seismic forces are first collected by each module's floor and ceiling, then passed through horizontal inter-module plates to the core or braced modules."],"answer":2,"explanation":"側向風力與地震力先由每個模組的樓板與天花板收集，再透過模組間的水平連接板傳到核心筒或斜撐模組。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wind and seismic forces are first collected by each module's floor and ceiling, then passed through horizontal inter-module plates to the core or braced modules. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b100-v13-06","title":"側向力傳遞、整體性與防連續倒塌：定量估算","titleEn":"Lateral load transfer, robustness and progressive collapse: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模組間水平繫結」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Inter-module horizontal ties” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：參考 EN 1991-1-7 附錄 A 的內部繫結型式 T = 0.8(g_k + ψq_k)·s·L，且不小於 75 kN。取 g_k = 4.0 kPa、ψq_k = 0.5×2.0 = 1.0 kPa、間距 s = 3.6 m、跨度 L = 12 m：T = 0.8×5.0×3.6×12 = 172.8 kN > 75 kN，故每處水平繫結須承受約 173 kN 拉力。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Following the internal-tie form of EN 1991-1-7 Annex A, T = 0.8(g_k + ψq_k)·s·L but not less than 75 kN. With g_k = 4.0 kPa, ψq_k = 0.5×2.0 = 1.0 kPa, spacing s = 3.6 m and span L = 12 m: T = 0.8×5.0×3.6×12 = 172.8 kN > 75 kN, so each horizontal tie must resist about 173 kN of tension. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以模型分析每一處模組間連接在風與地震下的剪力與拉力，並做移除單一模組的替代路徑分析；連接件以原型試驗確認強度與滑移，現場逐一檢查繫結板是否安裝、螺栓是否齊全。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Analyse shear and tension at every inter-module connection under wind and earthquake, and run alternate-path analysis with a single module removed; confirm connector strength and slip by prototype testing, and on site check one by one that tie plates are installed and every bolt is present.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"參考 EN 1991-1-7 附錄 A 的內部繫結型式 T = 0.8(g_k + ψq_k)·s·L，且不小於 75 kN。取 g_k = 4.0 kPa、ψq_k = 0.5×2.0 = 1.0 kPa、間距 s = 3.6 m、跨度 L = 12 m：T = 0.8×5.0×3.6×12 = 172.8 kN > 75 kN，故每處水平繫結須承受約 173 kN 拉力。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Following the internal-tie form of EN 1991-1-7 Annex A, T = 0.8(g_k + ψq_k)·s·L but not less than 75 kN. With g_k = 4.0 kPa, ψq_k = 0.5×2.0 = 1.0 kPa, spacing s = 3.6 m and span L = 12 m: T = 0.8×5.0×3.6×12 = 172.8 kN > 75 kN, so each horizontal tie must resist about 173 kN of tension. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「側向力傳遞、整體性與防連續倒塌」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lateral load transfer, robustness and progressive collapse\", which statement holds?","options":["參考 EN 1991-1-7 附錄 A 的內部繫結型式 T = 0.8(g_k + ψq_k)·s·L，且不小於 75 kN。","只要起重機額定荷重夠大，任何風速都可以吊模組。","模組在工廠製造，品質自然比工地好，不需要另外檢驗。"],"optionsEn":["Following the internal-tie form of EN 1991-1-7 Annex A, T = 0.8(g_k + ψq_k)·s·L but not less than 75 kN.","If the crane's rated capacity is large enough, modules can be lifted at any wind speed.","Factory-made modules are naturally better than site work, so no separate inspection is needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"參考 EN 1991-1-7 附錄 A 的內部繫結型式 T = 0.8(g_k + ψq_k)·s·L，且不小於 75 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Following the internal-tie form of EN 1991-1-7 Annex A, T = 0.8(g_k + ψq_k)·s·L but not less than 75 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b100-v13-07","title":"側向力傳遞、整體性與防連續倒塌：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lateral load transfer, robustness and progressive collapse: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模組間水平繫結」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Inter-module horizontal ties” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以模型分析每一處模組間連接在風與地震下的剪力與拉力，並做移除單一模組的替代路徑分析；連接件以原型試驗確認強度與滑移，現場逐一檢查繫結板是否安裝、螺栓是否齊全。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Analyse shear and tension at every inter-module connection under wind and earthquake, and run alternate-path analysis with a single module removed; confirm connector strength and slip by prototype testing, and on site check one by one that tie plates are installed and every bolt is present. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：結構設計須提出繫結配置圖與連續倒塌檢核，每一處繫結都是安裝保留點：未經檢查員確認繫結完成，不得在其上方繼續堆疊下一層模組。","observationEn":"Site practice: The structural design must provide a tie layout and progressive-collapse check, and every tie becomes an installation hold point: no further module may be stacked above until the inspector confirms the tie is complete.","failure":"注意干擾：為了方便安裝而省略部分模組間繫結，或把繫結板只以點焊臨時固定後忘記補強，正常使用時看不出問題，一旦發生瓦斯爆炸或車輛撞擊，局部破壞便可能沿著缺乏繫結的模組擴大。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting some inter-module ties for easier installation, or tack-welding tie plates temporarily and never completing them, shows nothing in normal use, but a gas explosion or vehicle impact can then spread local damage through the untied modules. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以模型分析每一處模組間連接在風與地震下的剪力與拉力，並做移除單一模組的替代路徑分析；連接件以原型試驗確認強度與滑移，現場逐一檢查繫結板是否安裝、螺栓是否齊全。","textEn":"Analyse shear and tension at every inter-module connection under wind and earthquake, and run alternate-path analysis with a single module removed; confirm connector strength and slip by prototype testing, and on site check one by one that tie plates are installed and every bolt is present.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"結構設計須提出繫結配置圖與連續倒塌檢核，每一處繫結都是安裝保留點：未經檢查員確認繫結完成，不得在其上方繼續堆疊下一層模組。","textEn":"The structural design must provide a tie layout and progressive-collapse check, and every tie becomes an installation hold point: no further module may be stacked above until the inspector confirms the tie is complete.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「側向力傳遞、整體性與防連續倒塌」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lateral load transfer, robustness and progressive collapse\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以模型分析每一處模組間連接在風與地震下的剪力與拉力，並做移除單一模組的替代路徑分析；連接件以原型試驗確認強度與滑移，現場逐一檢查繫結板是否安裝、螺栓是否齊全。","模組在工廠已做好防水，現場吊裝期間不需要另外防雨。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Analyse shear and tension at every inter-module connection under wind and earthquake, and run alternate-path analysis with a single module removed.","Modules are waterproofed in the factory, so no rain protection is needed during site installation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以模型分析每一處模組間連接在風與地震下的剪力與拉力，並做移除單一模組的替代路徑分析；連接件以原型試驗確認強度與滑移，現場逐一檢查繫結板是否安裝、螺栓是否齊全。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Analyse shear and tension at every inter-module connection under wind and earthquake, and run alternate-path analysis with a single module removed; confirm connector strength and slip by prototype testing, and on site check one by one that tie plates are installed and every bolt is present. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b100-v13-08","title":"側向力傳遞、整體性與防連續倒塌：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lateral load transfer, robustness and progressive collapse: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模組間水平繫結」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Inter-module horizontal ties” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為了方便安裝而省略部分模組間繫結，或把繫結板只以點焊臨時固定後忘記補強，正常使用時看不出問題，一旦發生瓦斯爆炸或車輛撞擊，局部破壞便可能沿著缺乏繫結的模組擴大。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting some inter-module ties for easier installation, or tack-welding tie plates temporarily and never completing them, shows nothing in normal use, but a gas explosion or vehicle impact can then spread local damage through the untied modules. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此設計要提供水平與垂直繫結，並檢核移除一個模組或一根角柱後，上方荷載能否由懸臂作用或繫結重新分配，這是模組建築防止連續倒塌的核心。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The design must therefore provide horizontal and vertical ties and check whether, with one module or corner post removed, the load above can be redistributed by cantilever action or ties; this is the core of preventing progressive collapse in modular buildings.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模組只要上下疊好，自重就足以讓建築維持整體性。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"As long as modules are stacked properly, self-weight alone keeps the building intact.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為了方便安裝而省略部分模組間繫結，或把繫結板只以點焊臨時固定後忘記補強，正常使用時看不出問題，一旦發生瓦斯爆炸或車輛撞擊，局部破壞便可能沿著缺乏繫結的模組擴大。","textEn":"Omitting some inter-module ties for easier installation, or tack-welding tie plates temporarily and never completing them, shows nothing in normal use, but a gas explosion or vehicle impact can then spread local damage through the untied modules.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側向力傳遞、整體性與防連續倒塌」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lateral load transfer, robustness and progressive collapse\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","模組接頭只要強度計算通過，安裝方式可以留給現場決定。","為了方便安裝而省略部分模組間繫結，或把繫結板只以點焊臨時固定後忘記補強，正常使用時看不出問題，一旦發生瓦斯爆炸或車輛撞擊，局部破壞便可能沿著缺乏繫結的模組擴大。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Once a module joint passes the strength calculation, how it is installed can be left to the site.","Omitting some inter-module ties for easier installation, or tack-welding tie plates temporarily and never completing them, shows nothing in normal use, but a gas explosion or vehicle impact can then spread local damage through the untied modules."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為了方便安裝而省略部分模組間繫結，或把繫結板只以點焊臨時固定後忘記補強，正常使用時看不出問題，一旦發生瓦斯爆炸或車輛撞擊，局部破壞便可能沿著缺乏繫結的模組擴大。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting some inter-module ties for easier installation, or tack-welding tie plates temporarily and never completing them, shows nothing in normal use, but a gas explosion or vehicle impact can then spread local damage through the untied modules. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b100-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「模組角部接頭與螺栓接合」與「吊點設計、吊具與模組變形」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Module corner joints and bolted connections\" and \"Lift points, lifting frames and module distortion\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b100-v13-09","title":"模組角部接頭與螺栓接合：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Module corner joints and bolted connections: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「角部定位錐與連接板」如何影響建築模組化吊裝與接合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Corner locating cones and plates” governs force, deformation or durability in “Volumetric modular-building lifting and connections”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"鋼構模組的角部接頭同時負責垂直定位與水平連接：常見做法是在下方模組頂部設定位錐或插銷，上方模組落下時自動對位，再以螺栓連接板把相鄰模組拉在一起。困難在於接頭位於模組內部或狹窄間隙中，螺栓必須能從外側、預留手孔或上一層施工面鎖固，否則既無法施作也無法檢查。混凝土 PPVC 則以預留鋼筋、續接器與灌漿形成濕式接頭，灌漿飽滿度是品質關鍵。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「角部定位錐與連接板」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Corner joints in steel modules provide both vertical location and horizontal connection: a common approach puts locating cones or pins on top of the lower module so the upper module self-aligns as it is lowered, then bolted plates pull adjacent modules together. The difficulty is that the joints sit inside modules or in narrow gaps, so bolts must be tightenable from outside, through access holes or from the next working level, or they can neither be installed nor inspected. Concrete PPVC uses projecting bars, couplers and grout to form wet joints, where complete grout filling is the key to quality. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Corner locating cones and plates” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：繫結力 172.8 kN 以 8.8 級 M20 螺栓單剪承擔，每支 F_v,Rd = 0.6×800×245/1.25 ≈ 94.1 kN，需 172.8/94.1 ≈ 1.84，取 2 支；若為了吸收公差改用長槽孔，承壓與滑移檢核更嚴，常需增加為 3 支或改用摩阻型接合。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Resisting the 172.8 kN tie force with grade 8.8 M20 bolts in single shear, each gives F_v,Rd = 0.6×800×245/1.25 ≈ 94.1 kN, so 172.8/94.1 ≈ 1.84 and two bolts are needed; long slotted holes used to absorb tolerances make bearing and slip checks stricter, often requiring three bolts or a slip-resistant connection.","failure":"常見誤解：「模組接頭只要強度計算通過，安裝方式可以留給現場決定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once a module joint passes the strength calculation, how it is installed can be left to the site.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「角部定位錐與連接板」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Corner locating cones and plates”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-09-k1","title":"模組角部接頭與螺栓接合","titleEn":"Module corner joints and bolted connections","text":"鋼構模組的角部接頭同時負責垂直定位與水平連接：常見做法是在下方模組頂部設定位錐或插銷，上方模組落下時自動對位，再以螺栓連接板把相鄰模組拉在一起。困難在於接頭位於模組內部或狹窄間隙中，螺栓必須能從外側、預留手孔或上一層施工面鎖固，否則既無法施作也無法檢查。","textEn":"Corner joints in steel modules provide both vertical location and horizontal connection: a common approach puts locating cones or pins on top of the lower module so the upper module self-aligns as it is lowered, then bolted plates pull adjacent modules together. The difficulty is that the joints sit inside modules or in narrow gaps, so bolts must be tightenable from outside, through access holes or from the next working level, or they can neither be installed nor inspected.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模組接頭只要強度計算通過，安裝方式可以留給現場決定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once a module joint passes the strength calculation, how it is installed can be left to the site. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模組角部接頭與螺栓接合」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Module corner joints and bolted connections\" is correct?","options":["鋼構模組的角部接頭同時負責垂直定位與水平連接：常見做法是在下方模組頂部設定位錐或插銷，上方模組落下時自動對位，再以螺栓連接板把相鄰模組拉在一起。","模組接頭只要強度計算通過，安裝方式可以留給現場決定。","模組既然能承受使用荷載，用任何方式吊起來都不會受損。"],"optionsEn":["Corner joints in steel modules provide both vertical location and horizontal connection: a common approach puts locating cones or pins on top of the lower module so the upper module self-aligns as it is lowered, then bolted plates pull adjacent modules together.","Once a module joint passes the strength calculation, how it is installed can be left to the site.","Since a module can carry service loads, any way of lifting it will do no harm."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鋼構模組的角部接頭同時負責垂直定位與水平連接：常見做法是在下方模組頂部設定位錐或插銷，上方模組落下時自動對位，再以螺栓連接板把相鄰模組拉在一起。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Corner joints in steel modules provide both vertical location and horizontal connection: a common approach puts locating cones or pins on top of the lower module so the upper module self-aligns as it is lowered, then bolted plates pull adjacent modules together. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b100-v13-10","title":"模組角部接頭與螺栓接合：定量估算","titleEn":"Module corner joints and bolted connections: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「角部定位錐與連接板」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Corner locating cones and plates” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：繫結力 172.8 kN 以 8.8 級 M20 螺栓單剪承擔，每支 F_v,Rd = 0.6×800×245/1.25 ≈ 94.1 kN，需 172.8/94.1 ≈ 1.84，取 2 支；若為了吸收公差改用長槽孔，承壓與滑移檢核更嚴，常需增加為 3 支或改用摩阻型接合。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Resisting the 172.8 kN tie force with grade 8.8 M20 bolts in single shear, each gives F_v,Rd = 0.6×800×245/1.25 ≈ 94.1 kN, so 172.8/94.1 ≈ 1.84 and two bolts are needed; long slotted holes used to absorb tolerances make bearing and slip checks stricter, often requiring three bolts or a slip-resistant connection. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以足尺接頭原型做拉力與剪力試驗，確認強度與滑移量；安裝後檢查螺栓數量、墊圈、鎖固順序與標記，混凝土接頭則以灌漿量紀錄、試體強度與必要時的非破壞檢測確認飽滿。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test full-scale joint prototypes in tension and shear to confirm strength and slip; after installation check bolt count, washers, tightening sequence and marking, and for concrete joints confirm complete filling from grout-volume records, cube strengths and non-destructive testing where needed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"繫結力 172.8 kN 以 8.8 級 M20 螺栓單剪承擔，每支 F_v,Rd = 0.6×800×245/1.25 ≈ 94.1 kN，需 172.8/94.1 ≈ 1.84，取 2 支；若為了吸收公差改用長槽孔，承壓與滑移檢核更嚴，常需增加為 3 支或改用摩阻型接合。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Resisting the 172.8 kN tie force with grade 8.8 M20 bolts in single shear, each gives F_v,Rd = 0.6×800×245/1.25 ≈ 94.1 kN, so 172.8/94.1 ≈ 1.84 and two bolts are needed; long slotted holes used to absorb tolerances make bearing and slip checks stricter, often requiring three bolts or a slip-resistant connection. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模組角部接頭與螺栓接合」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Module corner joints and bolted connections\", which statement holds?","options":["只要每個模組都在製造公差內，堆疊後整棟建築也必然在公差內。","繫結力 172.8 kN 以 8.8 級 M20 螺栓單剪承擔，每支 F_v,Rd = 0.6×800×245/1.25 ≈ 94.1 kN，需 172.8/94.1 ≈ 1.84，取 2 支。","扳手鎖到規定扭矩，就代表螺栓預拉力一定正確。"],"optionsEn":["If every module is within its fabrication tolerance, the stacked building must be too.","Resisting the 172.8 kN tie force with grade 8.8 M20 bolts in single shear, each gives F_v,Rd = 0.6×800×245/1.25 ≈ 94.1 kN, so 172.8/94.1 ≈ 1.84 and two bolts are needed.","Tightening to the specified torque guarantees the correct bolt preload."],"answer":1,"explanation":"繫結力 172.8 kN 以 8.8 級 M20 螺栓單剪承擔，每支 F_v,Rd = 0.6×800×245/1.25 ≈ 94.1 kN，需 172.8/94.1 ≈ 1.84，取 2 支；若為了吸收公差改用長槽孔，承壓與滑移檢核更嚴，常需增加為 3 支或改用摩阻型接合。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Resisting the 172.8 kN tie force with grade 8.8 M20 bolts in single shear, each gives F_v,Rd = 0.6×800×245/1.25 ≈ 94.1 kN, so 172.8/94.1 ≈ 1.84 and two bolts are needed; long slotted holes used to absorb tolerances make bearing and slip checks stricter, often requiring three bolts or a slip-resistant connection. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b100-v13-11","title":"模組角部接頭與螺栓接合：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Module corner joints and bolted connections: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「角部定位錐與連接板」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Corner locating cones and plates” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以足尺接頭原型做拉力與剪力試驗，確認強度與滑移量；安裝後檢查螺栓數量、墊圈、鎖固順序與標記，混凝土接頭則以灌漿量紀錄、試體強度與必要時的非破壞檢測確認飽滿。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test full-scale joint prototypes in tension and shear to confirm strength and slip; after installation check bolt count, washers, tightening sequence and marking, and for concrete joints confirm complete filling from grout-volume records, cube strengths and non-destructive testing where needed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：接頭設計要以三維模型檢查扳手與手孔的施工空間，並在工廠以實體樣品演練；任何接頭形式的變更都須由結構設計者重新簽認，並更新安裝程序書。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check wrench and access-hole space for every joint in the 3D model and rehearse it on a physical sample at the factory; any change to a joint type must be re-signed by the structural designer and reflected in the installation method statement.","failure":"注意干擾：接頭在圖面上可行，現場卻因相鄰模組的牆板擋住而放不進扳手，工人只好少鎖或改焊，接頭強度與可檢查性都無從保證；灌漿接頭若排氣不良留下空洞，鋼筋無法發揮錨定。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A joint that works on paper cannot take a wrench on site because the neighbouring module's wall panel is in the way, so workers fit fewer bolts or weld instead, leaving strength and inspectability unknown; a grouted joint with poor venting leaves voids so bars cannot develop anchorage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以足尺接頭原型做拉力與剪力試驗，確認強度與滑移量；安裝後檢查螺栓數量、墊圈、鎖固順序與標記，混凝土接頭則以灌漿量紀錄、試體強度與必要時的非破壞檢測確認飽滿。","textEn":"Test full-scale joint prototypes in tension and shear to confirm strength and slip; after installation check bolt count, washers, tightening sequence and marking, and for concrete joints confirm complete filling from grout-volume records, cube strengths and non-destructive testing where needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"接頭設計要以三維模型檢查扳手與手孔的施工空間，並在工廠以實體樣品演練；任何接頭形式的變更都須由結構設計者重新簽認，並更新安裝程序書。","textEn":"Check wrench and access-hole space for every joint in the 3D model and rehearse it on a physical sample at the factory; any change to a joint type must be re-signed by the structural designer and reflected in the installation method statement.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模組角部接頭與螺栓接合」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Module corner joints and bolted connections\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","模組建築完工後就與一般建築相同，不需要保存模組層級的資料。","以足尺接頭原型做拉力與剪力試驗，確認強度與滑移量；安裝後檢查螺栓數量、墊圈、鎖固順序與標記，混凝土接頭則以灌漿量紀錄、試體強度與必要時的非破壞檢測確認飽滿。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once completed, a modular building is like any other and needs no module-level records.","Test full-scale joint prototypes in tension and shear to confirm strength and slip."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以足尺接頭原型做拉力與剪力試驗，確認強度與滑移量；安裝後檢查螺栓數量、墊圈、鎖固順序與標記，混凝土接頭則以灌漿量紀錄、試體強度與必要時的非破壞檢測確認飽滿。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test full-scale joint prototypes in tension and shear to confirm strength and slip; after installation check bolt count, washers, tightening sequence and marking, and for concrete joints confirm complete filling from grout-volume records, cube strengths and non-destructive testing where needed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b100-v13-12","title":"模組角部接頭與螺栓接合：失效診斷","titleEn":"Module corner joints and bolted connections: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「角部定位錐與連接板」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Corner locating cones and plates” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接頭在圖面上可行，現場卻因相鄰模組的牆板擋住而放不進扳手，工人只好少鎖或改焊，接頭強度與可檢查性都無從保證；灌漿接頭若排氣不良留下空洞，鋼筋無法發揮錨定。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A joint that works on paper cannot take a wrench on site because the neighbouring module's wall panel is in the way, so workers fit fewer bolts or weld instead, leaving strength and inspectability unknown; a grouted joint with poor venting leaves voids so bars cannot develop anchorage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：混凝土 PPVC 則以預留鋼筋、續接器與灌漿形成濕式接頭，灌漿飽滿度是品質關鍵。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Concrete PPVC uses projecting bars, couplers and grout to form wet joints, where complete grout filling is the key to quality.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模組接頭只要強度計算通過，安裝方式可以留給現場決定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once a module joint passes the strength calculation, how it is installed can be left to the site.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接頭在圖面上可行，現場卻因相鄰模組的牆板擋住而放不進扳手，工人只好少鎖或改焊，接頭強度與可檢查性都無從保證；灌漿接頭若排氣不良留下空洞，鋼筋無法發揮錨定。","textEn":"A joint that works on paper cannot take a wrench on site because the neighbouring module's wall panel is in the way, so workers fit fewer bolts or weld instead, leaving strength and inspectability unknown; a grouted joint with poor venting leaves voids so bars cannot develop anchorage.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模組角部接頭與螺栓接合」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Module corner joints and bolted connections\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["接頭在圖面上可行，現場卻因相鄰模組的牆板擋住而放不進扳手，工人只好少鎖或改焊，接頭強度與可檢查性都無從保證；灌漿接頭若排氣不良留下空洞，鋼筋無法發揮錨定。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","模組既然能承受使用荷載，用任何方式吊起來都不會受損。"],"optionsEn":["A joint that works on paper cannot take a wrench on site because the neighbouring module's wall panel is in the way, so workers fit fewer bolts or weld instead, leaving strength and inspectability unknown.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Since a module can carry service loads, any way of lifting it will do no harm."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接頭在圖面上可行，現場卻因相鄰模組的牆板擋住而放不進扳手，工人只好少鎖或改焊，接頭強度與可檢查性都無從保證；灌漿接頭若排氣不良留下空洞，鋼筋無法發揮錨定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A joint that works on paper cannot take a wrench on site because the neighbouring module's wall panel is in the way, so workers fit fewer bolts or weld instead, leaving strength and inspectability unknown; a grouted joint with poor venting leaves voids so bars cannot develop anchorage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b100-v13-13","title":"吊點設計、吊具與模組變形：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Lift points, lifting frames and module distortion: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「吊點與吊裝框」如何影響建築模組化吊裝與接合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lift points and lifting frame” governs force, deformation or durability in “Volumetric modular-building lifting and connections”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"模組是大而薄的箱體，吊裝時的受力與使用時完全不同：若四條吊索直接斜拉到吊鉤，吊索的水平分力會向內壓擠模組頂框，可能使框架變形、牆板與裝修開裂，所以常用吊裝框或吊梁讓吊索保持垂直。浴室、廚房與機電設備使重心偏離幾何中心，吊起時模組會傾斜，需調整吊點或吊索長度。吊點與吊具屬於臨時工程，必須依起重相關標準設計、標示額定荷重並做荷重試驗。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「吊點與吊裝框」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A module is a large, thin box whose forces in lifting differ completely from those in service: four slings pulled straight to the hook push inward on the top frame with their horizontal components, which can distort the frame and crack wall panels and finishes, so a lifting frame or spreader beam keeps the slings vertical. Bathrooms, kitchens and plant shift the centre of gravity away from the geometric centre, so the module tilts when lifted unless lift points or sling lengths are adjusted. Lift points and lifting gear are temporary works that must be designed to lifting-equipment standards, marked with their rated load and load-tested. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Lift points and lifting frame” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：模組 25 t、動力係數 1.2，吊重 25×9.81×1.2 ≈ 294 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 25 t module with a dynamic factor of 1.2 gives a hook load of 25×9.81×1.2 ≈ 294 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「模組既然能承受使用荷載，用任何方式吊起來都不會受損。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Since a module can carry service loads, any way of lifting it will do no harm.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「吊點與吊裝框」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Lift points and lifting frame”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-13-k1","title":"吊點設計、吊具與模組變形","titleEn":"Lift points, lifting frames and module distortion","text":"模組是大而薄的箱體，吊裝時的受力與使用時完全不同：若四條吊索直接斜拉到吊鉤，吊索的水平分力會向內壓擠模組頂框，可能使框架變形、牆板與裝修開裂，所以常用吊裝框或吊梁讓吊索保持垂直。浴室、廚房與機電設備使重心偏離幾何中心，吊起時模組會傾斜，需調整吊點或吊索長度。","textEn":"A module is a large, thin box whose forces in lifting differ completely from those in service: four slings pulled straight to the hook push inward on the top frame with their horizontal components, which can distort the frame and crack wall panels and finishes, so a lifting frame or spreader beam keeps the slings vertical. Bathrooms, kitchens and plant shift the centre of gravity away from the geometric centre, so the module tilts when lifted unless lift points or sling lengths are adjusted.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模組既然能承受使用荷載，用任何方式吊起來都不會受損。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Since a module can carry service loads, any way of lifting it will do no harm. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「吊點設計、吊具與模組變形」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lift points, lifting frames and module distortion\" is correct?","options":["模組既然能承受使用荷載，用任何方式吊起來都不會受損。","模組是大而薄的箱體，吊裝時的受力與使用時完全不同：若四條吊索直接斜拉到吊鉤，吊索的水平分力會向內壓擠模組頂框，可能使框架變形、牆板與裝修開裂，所以常用吊裝框或吊梁讓吊索保持垂直。","只要起重機額定荷重夠大，任何風速都可以吊模組。"],"optionsEn":["Since a module can carry service loads, any way of lifting it will do no harm.","A module is a large, thin box whose forces in lifting differ completely from those in service: four slings pulled straight to the hook push inward on the top frame with their horizontal components, which can distort the frame and crack wall panels and finishes, so a lifting frame or spreader beam keeps the slings vertical.","If the crane's rated capacity is large enough, modules can be lifted at any wind speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"模組是大而薄的箱體，吊裝時的受力與使用時完全不同：若四條吊索直接斜拉到吊鉤，吊索的水平分力會向內壓擠模組頂框，可能使框架變形、牆板與裝修開裂，所以常用吊裝框或吊梁讓吊索保持垂直。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A module is a large, thin box whose forces in lifting differ completely from those in service: four slings pulled straight to the hook push inward on the top frame with their horizontal components, which can distort the frame and crack wall panels and finishes, so a lifting frame or spreader beam keeps the slings vertical. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b100-v13-14","title":"吊點設計、吊具與模組變形：定量估算","titleEn":"Lift points, lifting frames and module distortion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「吊點與吊裝框」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lift points and lifting frame” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：模組 25 t、動力係數 1.2，吊重 25×9.81×1.2 ≈ 294 kN。四肢吊索與水平成 60° 時，每肢張力 T = 294/(4 sin 60°) ≈ 85.0 kN，水平分力 T cos 60° ≈ 42.5 kN 向內壓擠頂框；改用吊裝框使吊索垂直後，每肢 294/4 ≈ 73.6 kN，水平分力趨近 0。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 25 t module with a dynamic factor of 1.2 gives a hook load of 25×9.81×1.2 ≈ 294 kN. With four sling legs at 60° to the horizontal, each leg carries T = 294/(4 sin 60°) ≈ 85.0 kN and its horizontal component T cos 60° ≈ 42.5 kN squeezes the top frame inward; a lifting frame that keeps slings vertical gives 294/4 ≈ 73.6 kN per leg with nearly zero horizontal component. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：吊點以計算與荷重試驗確認，吊裝框依 EN 13155 一類標準設計並標示額定荷重與自重；每種模組型式在工廠先試吊，量測離地後的傾斜角與框架變形並與重心計算比較，調整後才放行運送。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm lift points by calculation and load test, design the lifting frame to standards such as EN 13155 and mark it with rated load and self-weight; trial-lift each module type at the factory, measuring tilt and frame distortion once clear of the ground against the centre-of-gravity calculation, and release it for shipping only after adjustment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"模組 25 t、動力係數 1.2，吊重 25×9.81×1.2 ≈ 294 kN。四肢吊索與水平成 60° 時，每肢張力 T = 294/(4 sin 60°) ≈ 85.0 kN，水平分力 T cos 60° ≈ 42.5 kN 向內壓擠頂框；改用吊裝框使吊索垂直後，每肢 294/4 ≈ 73.6 kN，水平分力趨近 0。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A 25 t module with a dynamic factor of 1.2 gives a hook load of 25×9.81×1.2 ≈ 294 kN. With four sling legs at 60° to the horizontal, each leg carries T = 294/(4 sin 60°) ≈ 85.0 kN and its horizontal component T cos 60° ≈ 42.5 kN squeezes the top frame inward; a lifting frame that keeps slings vertical gives 294/4 ≈ 73.6 kN per leg with nearly zero horizontal component. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「吊點設計、吊具與模組變形」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lift points, lifting frames and module distortion\", which statement holds?","options":["模組在工廠製造，品質自然比工地好，不需要另外檢驗。","模組在工廠已做好防水，現場吊裝期間不需要另外防雨。","模組 25 t、動力係數 1.2，吊重 25×9.81×1.2 ≈ 294 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Factory-made modules are naturally better than site work, so no separate inspection is needed.","Modules are waterproofed in the factory, so no rain protection is needed during site installation.","A 25 t module with a dynamic factor of 1.2 gives a hook load of 25×9.81×1.2 ≈ 294 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模組 25 t、動力係數 1.2，吊重 25×9.81×1.2 ≈ 294 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 25 t module with a dynamic factor of 1.2 gives a hook load of 25×9.81×1.2 ≈ 294 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b100-v13-15","title":"吊點設計、吊具與模組變形：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lift points, lifting frames and module distortion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「吊點與吊裝框」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lift points and lifting frame” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"吊點以計算與荷重試驗確認，吊裝框依 EN 13155 一類標準設計並標示額定荷重與自重；每種模組型式在工廠先試吊，量測離地後的傾斜角與框架變形並與重心計算比較，調整後才放行運送。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm lift points by calculation and load test, design the lifting frame to standards such as EN 13155 and mark it with rated load and self-weight; trial-lift each module type at the factory, measuring tilt and frame distortion once clear of the ground against the centre-of-gravity calculation, and release it for shipping only after adjustment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：每種模組都要有吊裝計算書與吊點圖，標示重量、重心與吊具配置；吊具須有荷重試驗證明與定期檢查紀錄，吊裝計畫由合格的吊掛負責人簽核，現場依核准的計畫作業。","observationEn":"Site practice: Every module type needs a lifting calculation and lift-point drawing showing weight, centre of gravity and rigging arrangement; lifting gear needs load-test certificates and periodic inspection records, and the lifting plan is signed by a competent lifting supervisor and followed as approved on site.","failure":"注意干擾：未用吊裝框而直接斜拉吊索，模組頂框被壓彎，落位後門框變形、石膏板接縫開裂；重心估算錯誤使模組在高空傾斜，接近定位時撞擊已安裝的模組，造成損壞並威脅下方人員。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Slinging directly at an angle without a lifting frame bends the module's top frame, so after setting the door frames are distorted and plasterboard joints crack; a wrong centre-of-gravity estimate tilts the module at height so it strikes already-installed modules on approach, causing damage and endangering people below. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"吊點以計算與荷重試驗確認，吊裝框依 EN 13155 一類標準設計並標示額定荷重與自重；每種模組型式在工廠先試吊，量測離地後的傾斜角與框架變形並與重心計算比較，調整後才放行運送。","textEn":"Confirm lift points by calculation and load test, design the lifting frame to standards such as EN 13155 and mark it with rated load and self-weight; trial-lift each module type at the factory, measuring tilt and frame distortion once clear of the ground against the centre-of-gravity calculation, and release it for shipping only after adjustment.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"每種模組都要有吊裝計算書與吊點圖，標示重量、重心與吊具配置；吊具須有荷重試驗證明與定期檢查紀錄，吊裝計畫由合格的吊掛負責人簽核，現場依核准的計畫作業。","textEn":"Every module type needs a lifting calculation and lift-point drawing showing weight, centre of gravity and rigging arrangement; lifting gear needs load-test certificates and periodic inspection records, and the lifting plan is signed by a competent lifting supervisor and followed as approved on site.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「吊點設計、吊具與模組變形」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lift points, lifting frames and module distortion\"?","options":["吊點以計算與荷重試驗確認，吊裝框依 EN 13155 一類標準設計並標示額定荷重與自重。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","模組在工廠已經做好結構，堆疊後不需要整體結構分析。"],"optionsEn":["Confirm lift points by calculation and load test, design the lifting frame to standards such as EN 13155 and mark it with rated load and self-weight.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Since each module's structure is finished in the factory, the stacked building needs no overall structural analysis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"吊點以計算與荷重試驗確認，吊裝框依 EN 13155 一類標準設計並標示額定荷重與自重；每種模組型式在工廠先試吊，量測離地後的傾斜角與框架變形並與重心計算比較，調整後才放行運送。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm lift points by calculation and load test, design the lifting frame to standards such as EN 13155 and mark it with rated load and self-weight; trial-lift each module type at the factory, measuring tilt and frame distortion once clear of the ground against the centre-of-gravity calculation, and release it for shipping only after adjustment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b100-v13-16","title":"吊點設計、吊具與模組變形：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lift points, lifting frames and module distortion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「吊點與吊裝框」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lift points and lifting frame” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未用吊裝框而直接斜拉吊索，模組頂框被壓彎，落位後門框變形、石膏板接縫開裂；重心估算錯誤使模組在高空傾斜，接近定位時撞擊已安裝的模組，造成損壞並威脅下方人員。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Slinging directly at an angle without a lifting frame bends the module's top frame, so after setting the door frames are distorted and plasterboard joints crack; a wrong centre-of-gravity estimate tilts the module at height so it strikes already-installed modules on approach, causing damage and endangering people below. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：吊點與吊具屬於臨時工程，必須依起重相關標準設計、標示額定荷重並做荷重試驗。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Lift points and lifting gear are temporary works that must be designed to lifting-equipment standards, marked with their rated load and load-tested.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模組既然能承受使用荷載，用任何方式吊起來都不會受損。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Since a module can carry service loads, any way of lifting it will do no harm.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未用吊裝框而直接斜拉吊索，模組頂框被壓彎，落位後門框變形、石膏板接縫開裂；重心估算錯誤使模組在高空傾斜，接近定位時撞擊已安裝的模組，造成損壞並威脅下方人員。","textEn":"Slinging directly at an angle without a lifting frame bends the module's top frame, so after setting the door frames are distorted and plasterboard joints crack; a wrong centre-of-gravity estimate tilts the module at height so it strikes already-installed modules on approach, causing damage and endangering people below.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「吊點設計、吊具與模組變形」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lift points, lifting frames and module distortion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","未用吊裝框而直接斜拉吊索，模組頂框被壓彎，落位後門框變形、石膏板接縫開裂；重心估算錯誤使模組在高空傾斜，接近定位時撞擊已安裝的模組，造成損壞並威脅下方人員。","只要起重機額定荷重夠大，任何風速都可以吊模組。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Slinging directly at an angle without a lifting frame bends the module's top frame, so after setting the door frames are distorted and plasterboard joints crack.","If the crane's rated capacity is large enough, modules can be lifted at any wind speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未用吊裝框而直接斜拉吊索，模組頂框被壓彎，落位後門框變形、石膏板接縫開裂；重心估算錯誤使模組在高空傾斜，接近定位時撞擊已安裝的模組，造成損壞並威脅下方人員。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Slinging directly at an angle without a lifting frame bends the module's top frame, so after setting the door frames are distorted and plasterboard joints crack; a wrong centre-of-gravity estimate tilts the module at height so it strikes already-installed modules on approach, causing damage and endangering people below. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b100-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「起重機選型、吊裝順序與風速限制」與「堆疊公差、墊片與垂直度控制」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Crane selection, lifting sequence and wind limits\" and \"Stacking tolerances, shims and verticality control\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b100-v13-17","title":"起重機選型、吊裝順序與風速限制：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Crane selection, lifting sequence and wind limits: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「起重半徑與受風面積」如何影響建築模組化吊裝與接合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Crane radius and wind area” governs force, deformation or durability in “Volumetric modular-building lifting and connections”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"模組重量集中、外形大，起重機選型要同時考慮吊重、半徑與吊高，最遠、最重的模組通常決定起重機規格。模組像一面帆，受風面積遠大於鋼梁，風會讓吊在空中的模組旋轉與擺動，使定位困難並可能撞擊結構，所以模組吊裝的允許風速通常低於一般吊裝。吊裝順序要讓結構在每個階段都穩定，並配合即時進場的運輸排程，減少工地堆置。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「起重半徑與受風面積」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Modules are heavy and bulky, so crane selection must consider load, radius and hook height together, and the farthest, heaviest module usually sets the crane size. A module acts like a sail with far more wind area than a steel beam, so wind turns and swings it in the air, making placement difficult and risking impact with the structure; module lifting therefore usually has a lower permissible wind speed than ordinary lifting. The lifting sequence must keep the structure stable at every stage and match just-in-time delivery to minimise storage on site. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Crane radius and wind area” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：模組受風面積 12 m × 3.2 m = 38.4 m²，C_d = 1.2、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³：風速 10 m/s 時 F = 0.5×1.25×10²×1.2×38.4 = 2,880 N，15 m/s 時 6,480 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A module face of 12 m × 3.2 m = 38.4 m² with C_d = 1.2 and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³ takes F = 0.5×1.25×10²×1.2×38.4 = 2,880 N at 10 m/s and 6,480 N at 15 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要起重機額定荷重夠大，任何風速都可以吊模組。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the crane's rated capacity is large enough, modules can be lifted at any wind speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「起重半徑與受風面積」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Crane radius and wind area”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-17-k1","title":"起重機選型、吊裝順序與風速限制","titleEn":"Crane selection, lifting sequence and wind limits","text":"模組重量集中、外形大，起重機選型要同時考慮吊重、半徑與吊高，最遠、最重的模組通常決定起重機規格。模組像一面帆，受風面積遠大於鋼梁，風會讓吊在空中的模組旋轉與擺動，使定位困難並可能撞擊結構，所以模組吊裝的允許風速通常低於一般吊裝。","textEn":"Modules are heavy and bulky, so crane selection must consider load, radius and hook height together, and the farthest, heaviest module usually sets the crane size. A module acts like a sail with far more wind area than a steel beam, so wind turns and swings it in the air, making placement difficult and risking impact with the structure; module lifting therefore usually has a lower permissible wind speed than ordinary lifting.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要起重機額定荷重夠大，任何風速都可以吊模組。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the crane's rated capacity is large enough, modules can be lifted at any wind speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「起重機選型、吊裝順序與風速限制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Crane selection, lifting sequence and wind limits\" is correct?","options":["只要起重機額定荷重夠大，任何風速都可以吊模組。","只要每個模組都在製造公差內，堆疊後整棟建築也必然在公差內。","模組重量集中、外形大，起重機選型要同時考慮吊重、半徑與吊高，最遠、最重的模組通常決定起重機規格。"],"optionsEn":["If the crane's rated capacity is large enough, modules can be lifted at any wind speed.","If every module is within its fabrication tolerance, the stacked building must be too.","Modules are heavy and bulky, so crane selection must consider load, radius and hook height together, and the farthest, heaviest module usually sets the crane size."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模組重量集中、外形大，起重機選型要同時考慮吊重、半徑與吊高，最遠、最重的模組通常決定起重機規格。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Modules are heavy and bulky, so crane selection must consider load, radius and hook height together, and the farthest, heaviest module usually sets the crane size. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b100-v13-18","title":"起重機選型、吊裝順序與風速限制：定量估算","titleEn":"Crane selection, lifting sequence and wind limits: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「起重半徑與受風面積」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Crane radius and wind area” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：模組受風面積 12 m × 3.2 m = 38.4 m²，C_d = 1.2、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³：風速 10 m/s 時 F = 0.5×1.25×10²×1.2×38.4 = 2,880 N，15 m/s 時 6,480 N。相對於 25 t（約 245 kN）的重量，偏擺角約 atan(6.48/245) ≈ 1.5°，吊索長 40 m 時水平偏移約 40×6.48/245 ≈ 1.06 m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A module face of 12 m × 3.2 m = 38.4 m² with C_d = 1.2 and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³ takes F = 0.5×1.25×10²×1.2×38.4 = 2,880 N at 10 m/s and 6,480 N at 15 m/s. Against a 25 t weight of about 245 kN the swing angle is about atan(6.48/245) ≈ 1.5°, so with 40 m of hoist rope the horizontal offset is about 40×6.48/245 ≈ 1.06 m. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：吊裝前核對每一模組的出廠秤重、吊具重量與半徑，對照起重機荷重表；現場以風速計在吊高處量測陣風，超過計畫門檻即暫停；每次吊裝記錄模組編號、重量、風速與定位時間，作為後續吊次規劃依據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before lifting, check each module's weighed factory mass, rigging weight and radius against the crane load chart; measure gusts at hook height with an anemometer and stop when the planned limit is exceeded; record module number, weight, wind speed and placement time for every lift to inform later lift planning.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"模組受風面積 12 m × 3.2 m = 38.4 m²，C_d = 1.2、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³：風速 10 m/s 時 F = 0.5×1.25×10²×1.2×38.4 = 2,880 N，15 m/s 時 6,480 N。相對於 25 t（約 245 kN）的重量，偏擺角約 atan(6.48/245) ≈ 1.5°，吊索長 40 m 時水平偏移約 40×6.48/245 ≈ 1.06 m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A module face of 12 m × 3.2 m = 38.4 m² with C_d = 1.2 and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³ takes F = 0.5×1.25×10²×1.2×38.4 = 2,880 N at 10 m/s and 6,480 N at 15 m/s. Against a 25 t weight of about 245 kN the swing angle is about atan(6.48/245) ≈ 1.5°, so with 40 m of hoist rope the horizontal offset is about 40×6.48/245 ≈ 1.06 m. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「起重機選型、吊裝順序與風速限制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Crane selection, lifting sequence and wind limits\", which statement holds?","options":["模組受風面積 12 m × 3.2 m = 38.4 m²，C_d = 1.2、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³：風速 10 m/s 時 F = 0.5×1.25×10²×1.2×38.4 = 2,880 N，15 m/s 時 6,480 N。","扳手鎖到規定扭矩，就代表螺栓預拉力一定正確。","模組建築完工後就與一般建築相同，不需要保存模組層級的資料。"],"optionsEn":["A module face of 12 m × 3.2 m = 38.4 m² with C_d = 1.2 and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³ takes F = 0.5×1.25×10²×1.2×38.4 = 2,880 N at 10 m/s and 6,480 N at 15 m/s.","Tightening to the specified torque guarantees the correct bolt preload.","Once completed, a modular building is like any other and needs no module-level records."],"answer":0,"explanation":"模組受風面積 12 m × 3.2 m = 38.4 m²，C_d = 1.2、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³：風速 10 m/s 時 F = 0.5×1.25×10²×1.2×38.4 = 2,880 N，15 m/s 時 6,480 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A module face of 12 m × 3.2 m = 38.4 m² with C_d = 1.2 and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³ takes F = 0.5×1.25×10²×1.2×38.4 = 2,880 N at 10 m/s and 6,480 N at 15 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b100-v13-19","title":"起重機選型、吊裝順序與風速限制：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Crane selection, lifting sequence and wind limits: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「起重半徑與受風面積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Crane radius and wind area” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"吊裝前核對每一模組的出廠秤重、吊具重量與半徑，對照起重機荷重表；現場以風速計在吊高處量測陣風，超過計畫門檻即暫停；每次吊裝記錄模組編號、重量、風速與定位時間，作為後續吊次規劃依據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before lifting, check each module's weighed factory mass, rigging weight and radius against the crane load chart; measure gusts at hook height with an anemometer and stop when the planned limit is exceeded; record module number, weight, wind speed and placement time for every lift to inform later lift planning. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：吊裝計畫須列出每一吊次的重量、半徑、使用率、允許風速、牽引繩配置與禁區，經吊掛負責人與工地主任核准；風速、能見度或通訊不符條件時，吊掛負責人有權也有義務停止作業。","observationEn":"Site practice: The lifting plan must list weight, radius, utilisation, permissible wind speed, tag-line arrangement and exclusion zone for every lift, approved by the lifting supervisor and site manager; when wind, visibility or communications fall outside the conditions, the lifting supervisor has both the authority and the duty to stop work.","failure":"注意干擾：以設計重量而非出廠秤重規劃吊次，裝修與設備增加的重量使部分吊次超過起重機在該半徑的能力；在陣風中勉強吊裝，模組旋轉撞擊鷹架，拉牽引繩的工人被拖行受傷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Planning lifts from design weights instead of weighed factory masses lets added finishes and equipment push some lifts beyond the crane's capacity at that radius; forcing a lift in gusts spins the module into scaffolding and drags tag-line workers, injuring them. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"吊裝前核對每一模組的出廠秤重、吊具重量與半徑，對照起重機荷重表；現場以風速計在吊高處量測陣風，超過計畫門檻即暫停；每次吊裝記錄模組編號、重量、風速與定位時間，作為後續吊次規劃依據。","textEn":"Before lifting, check each module's weighed factory mass, rigging weight and radius against the crane load chart; measure gusts at hook height with an anemometer and stop when the planned limit is exceeded; record module number, weight, wind speed and placement time for every lift to inform later lift planning.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"吊裝計畫須列出每一吊次的重量、半徑、使用率、允許風速、牽引繩配置與禁區，經吊掛負責人與工地主任核准；風速、能見度或通訊不符條件時，吊掛負責人有權也有義務停止作業。","textEn":"The lifting plan must list weight, radius, utilisation, permissible wind speed, tag-line arrangement and exclusion zone for every lift, approved by the lifting supervisor and site manager; when wind, visibility or communications fall outside the conditions, the lifting supervisor has both the authority and the duty to stop work.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「起重機選型、吊裝順序與風速限制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Crane selection, lifting sequence and wind limits\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","吊裝前核對每一模組的出廠秤重、吊具重量與半徑，對照起重機荷重表。","模組只要上下疊好，自重就足以讓建築維持整體性。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Before lifting, check each module's weighed factory mass, rigging weight and radius against the crane load chart.","As long as modules are stacked properly, self-weight alone keeps the building intact."],"answer":1,"explanation":"吊裝前核對每一模組的出廠秤重、吊具重量與半徑，對照起重機荷重表；現場以風速計在吊高處量測陣風，超過計畫門檻即暫停；每次吊裝記錄模組編號、重量、風速與定位時間，作為後續吊次規劃依據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before lifting, check each module's weighed factory mass, rigging weight and radius against the crane load chart; measure gusts at hook height with an anemometer and stop when the planned limit is exceeded; record module number, weight, wind speed and placement time for every lift to inform later lift planning. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b100-v13-20","title":"起重機選型、吊裝順序與風速限制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Crane selection, lifting sequence and wind limits: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「起重半徑與受風面積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Crane radius and wind area” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以設計重量而非出廠秤重規劃吊次，裝修與設備增加的重量使部分吊次超過起重機在該半徑的能力；在陣風中勉強吊裝，模組旋轉撞擊鷹架，拉牽引繩的工人被拖行受傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Planning lifts from design weights instead of weighed factory masses lets added finishes and equipment push some lifts beyond the crane's capacity at that radius; forcing a lift in gusts spins the module into scaffolding and drags tag-line workers, injuring them. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：吊裝順序要讓結構在每個階段都穩定，並配合即時進場的運輸排程，減少工地堆置。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The lifting sequence must keep the structure stable at every stage and match just-in-time delivery to minimise storage on site.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要起重機額定荷重夠大，任何風速都可以吊模組。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the crane's rated capacity is large enough, modules can be lifted at any wind speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以設計重量而非出廠秤重規劃吊次，裝修與設備增加的重量使部分吊次超過起重機在該半徑的能力；在陣風中勉強吊裝，模組旋轉撞擊鷹架，拉牽引繩的工人被拖行受傷。","textEn":"Planning lifts from design weights instead of weighed factory masses lets added finishes and equipment push some lifts beyond the crane's capacity at that radius; forcing a lift in gusts spins the module into scaffolding and drags tag-line workers, injuring them.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「起重機選型、吊裝順序與風速限制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Crane selection, lifting sequence and wind limits\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","只要每個模組都在製造公差內，堆疊後整棟建築也必然在公差內。","以設計重量而非出廠秤重規劃吊次，裝修與設備增加的重量使部分吊次超過起重機在該半徑的能力；在陣風中勉強吊裝，模組旋轉撞擊鷹架，拉牽引繩的工人被拖行受傷。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","If every module is within its fabrication tolerance, the stacked building must be too.","Planning lifts from design weights instead of weighed factory masses lets added finishes and equipment push some lifts beyond the crane's capacity at that radius."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以設計重量而非出廠秤重規劃吊次，裝修與設備增加的重量使部分吊次超過起重機在該半徑的能力；在陣風中勉強吊裝，模組旋轉撞擊鷹架，拉牽引繩的工人被拖行受傷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Planning lifts from design weights instead of weighed factory masses lets added finishes and equipment push some lifts beyond the crane's capacity at that radius; forcing a lift in gusts spins the module into scaffolding and drags tag-line workers, injuring them. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b100-v13-21","title":"堆疊公差、墊片與垂直度控制：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Stacking tolerances, shims and verticality control: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「墊片與堆疊標高」如何影響建築模組化吊裝與接合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shims and stack levels” governs force, deformation or durability in “Volumetric modular-building lifting and connections”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"每個模組出廠時都有高度、長度與方正度的製造公差，堆疊時這些偏差會逐層累積，墊塊壓縮、接頭間隙與裙樓轉換層的平整度也會加入。若不控制，高樓層模組的樓板會越來越不水平、外牆線條歪斜，帷幕或外牆板接縫寬度失控。因此安裝時每隔幾層就要量測標高與垂直度並以墊片修正，裙樓或轉換層頂面的精度要求也必須比一般樓板嚴格。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「墊片與堆疊標高」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Every module leaves the factory with height, length and squareness tolerances, and in stacking these deviations accumulate floor by floor, joined by packer compression, joint gaps and the flatness of the podium or transfer level. Uncontrolled, upper module floors drift out of level, façade lines lean and cladding joint widths run out of control. Installation therefore measures level and verticality every few storeys and corrects with shims, and the top of the podium or transfer level needs tighter accuracy than an ordinary slab. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Shims and stack levels” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：每個模組高度公差 ±3 mm、堆疊 30 層：最壞情況累積 30×3 = 90 mm，隨機合成約 √30×3 ≈ 16.4 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With ±3 mm height tolerance per module over 30 storeys, worst-case accumulation is 30×3 = 90 mm and random combination about √30×3 ≈ 16.4 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要每個模組都在製造公差內，堆疊後整棟建築也必然在公差內。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If every module is within its fabrication tolerance, the stacked building must be too.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「墊片與堆疊標高」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Shims and stack levels”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-21-k1","title":"堆疊公差、墊片與垂直度控制","titleEn":"Stacking tolerances, shims and verticality control","text":"每個模組出廠時都有高度、長度與方正度的製造公差，堆疊時這些偏差會逐層累積，墊塊壓縮、接頭間隙與裙樓轉換層的平整度也會加入。若不控制，高樓層模組的樓板會越來越不水平、外牆線條歪斜，帷幕或外牆板接縫寬度失控。","textEn":"Every module leaves the factory with height, length and squareness tolerances, and in stacking these deviations accumulate floor by floor, joined by packer compression, joint gaps and the flatness of the podium or transfer level. Uncontrolled, upper module floors drift out of level, façade lines lean and cladding joint widths run out of control.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要每個模組都在製造公差內，堆疊後整棟建築也必然在公差內。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If every module is within its fabrication tolerance, the stacked building must be too. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「堆疊公差、墊片與垂直度控制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stacking tolerances, shims and verticality control\" is correct?","options":["每個模組出廠時都有高度、長度與方正度的製造公差，堆疊時這些偏差會逐層累積，墊塊壓縮、接頭間隙與裙樓轉換層的平整度也會加入。","只要每個模組都在製造公差內，堆疊後整棟建築也必然在公差內。","模組在工廠製造，品質自然比工地好，不需要另外檢驗。"],"optionsEn":["Every module leaves the factory with height, length and squareness tolerances, and in stacking these deviations accumulate floor by floor, joined by packer compression, joint gaps and the flatness of the podium or transfer level.","If every module is within its fabrication tolerance, the stacked building must be too.","Factory-made modules are naturally better than site work, so no separate inspection is needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每個模組出廠時都有高度、長度與方正度的製造公差，堆疊時這些偏差會逐層累積，墊塊壓縮、接頭間隙與裙樓轉換層的平整度也會加入。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Every module leaves the factory with height, length and squareness tolerances, and in stacking these deviations accumulate floor by floor, joined by packer compression, joint gaps and the flatness of the podium or transfer level. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b100-v13-22","title":"堆疊公差、墊片與垂直度控制：定量估算","titleEn":"Stacking tolerances, shims and verticality control: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「墊片與堆疊標高」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shims and stack levels” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：每個模組高度公差 ±3 mm、堆疊 30 層：最壞情況累積 30×3 = 90 mm，隨機合成約 √30×3 ≈ 16.4 mm。若墊塊壓縮比預期少而每層系統偏高 +1 mm，30 層再加 30 mm，隨機與系統合計可能超出外牆接縫 ±20 mm 的調整範圍，所以每 5 層以墊片歸零一次。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With ±3 mm height tolerance per module over 30 storeys, worst-case accumulation is 30×3 = 90 mm and random combination about √30×3 ≈ 16.4 mm. If packers compress less than expected so each storey sits 1 mm high, 30 storeys add 30 mm systematically, and random plus systematic error may exceed a ±20 mm façade joint adjustment range, so levels are reset with shims every five storeys. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每安裝一層，以全測站量測模組角點的標高與平面位置，計算與設計的偏差並繪成趨勢；每 5 層做一次整體垂直度與標高檢核，結果連動下一批模組的墊片厚度計畫，並在開始堆疊前先驗收裙樓頂面。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After each level, measure corner levels and plan positions with a total station, compute deviations from design and plot the trend; every five storeys check overall verticality and level, link the results to the shim plan for the next batch, and accept the podium top surface before stacking starts.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"每個模組高度公差 ±3 mm、堆疊 30 層：最壞情況累積 30×3 = 90 mm，隨機合成約 √30×3 ≈ 16.4 mm。若墊塊壓縮比預期少而每層系統偏高 +1 mm，30 層再加 30 mm，隨機與系統合計可能超出外牆接縫 ±20 mm 的調整範圍，所以每 5 層以墊片歸零一次。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With ±3 mm height tolerance per module over 30 storeys, worst-case accumulation is 30×3 = 90 mm and random combination about √30×3 ≈ 16.4 mm. If packers compress less than expected so each storey sits 1 mm high, 30 storeys add 30 mm systematically, and random plus systematic error may exceed a ±20 mm façade joint adjustment range, so levels are reset with shims every five storeys. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「堆疊公差、墊片與垂直度控制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stacking tolerances, shims and verticality control\", which statement holds?","options":["模組在工廠已做好防水，現場吊裝期間不需要另外防雨。","每個模組高度公差 ±3 mm、堆疊 30 層：最壞情況累積 30×3 = 90 mm，隨機合成約 √30×3 ≈ 16.4 mm。","模組在工廠已經做好結構，堆疊後不需要整體結構分析。"],"optionsEn":["Modules are waterproofed in the factory, so no rain protection is needed during site installation.","With ±3 mm height tolerance per module over 30 storeys, worst-case accumulation is 30×3 = 90 mm and random combination about √30×3 ≈ 16.4 mm.","Since each module's structure is finished in the factory, the stacked building needs no overall structural analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每個模組高度公差 ±3 mm、堆疊 30 層：最壞情況累積 30×3 = 90 mm，隨機合成約 √30×3 ≈ 16.4 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With ±3 mm height tolerance per module over 30 storeys, worst-case accumulation is 30×3 = 90 mm and random combination about √30×3 ≈ 16.4 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b100-v13-23","title":"堆疊公差、墊片與垂直度控制：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stacking tolerances, shims and verticality control: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「墊片與堆疊標高」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shims and stack levels” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每安裝一層，以全測站量測模組角點的標高與平面位置，計算與設計的偏差並繪成趨勢；每 5 層做一次整體垂直度與標高檢核，結果連動下一批模組的墊片厚度計畫，並在開始堆疊前先驗收裙樓頂面。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After each level, measure corner levels and plan positions with a total station, compute deviations from design and plot the trend; every five storeys check overall verticality and level, link the results to the shim plan for the next batch, and accept the podium top surface before stacking starts. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：安裝程序書應規定量測頻率、墊片材料與最大厚度、歸零樓層與允許偏差；裙樓頂面驗收列為開始堆疊前的保留點，由測量主管與結構設計者共同簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The installation method statement must set measurement frequency, shim material and maximum thickness, reset levels and permitted deviations, with podium acceptance as a hold point before stacking begins, signed jointly by the survey lead and the structural designer.","failure":"注意干擾：裙樓轉換層頂面不平而未先修正，第一層模組就帶著傾斜，後續每層依前一層對位使傾斜延續到頂部，帷幕外牆接縫上寬下窄，只能在高樓層以異形板件收邊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An uneven podium transfer slab left uncorrected tilts the first module level, each later level aligns to the one below so the tilt continues to the roof, and façade joints widen toward the top, ending in special-shaped closure panels at high level. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每安裝一層，以全測站量測模組角點的標高與平面位置，計算與設計的偏差並繪成趨勢；每 5 層做一次整體垂直度與標高檢核，結果連動下一批模組的墊片厚度計畫，並在開始堆疊前先驗收裙樓頂面。","textEn":"After each level, measure corner levels and plan positions with a total station, compute deviations from design and plot the trend; every five storeys check overall verticality and level, link the results to the shim plan for the next batch, and accept the podium top surface before stacking starts.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"安裝程序書應規定量測頻率、墊片材料與最大厚度、歸零樓層與允許偏差；裙樓頂面驗收列為開始堆疊前的保留點，由測量主管與結構設計者共同簽認。","textEn":"The installation method statement must set measurement frequency, shim material and maximum thickness, reset levels and permitted deviations, with podium acceptance as a hold point before stacking begins, signed jointly by the survey lead and the structural designer.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「堆疊公差、墊片與垂直度控制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stacking tolerances, shims and verticality control\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","模組接頭只要強度計算通過，安裝方式可以留給現場決定。","每安裝一層，以全測站量測模組角點的標高與平面位置，計算與設計的偏差並繪成趨勢。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Once a module joint passes the strength calculation, how it is installed can be left to the site.","After each level, measure corner levels and plan positions with a total station, compute deviations from design and plot the trend."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每安裝一層，以全測站量測模組角點的標高與平面位置，計算與設計的偏差並繪成趨勢；每 5 層做一次整體垂直度與標高檢核，結果連動下一批模組的墊片厚度計畫，並在開始堆疊前先驗收裙樓頂面。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After each level, measure corner levels and plan positions with a total station, compute deviations from design and plot the trend; every five storeys check overall verticality and level, link the results to the shim plan for the next batch, and accept the podium top surface before stacking starts. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b100-v13-24","title":"堆疊公差、墊片與垂直度控制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stacking tolerances, shims and verticality control: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「墊片與堆疊標高」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shims and stack levels” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"裙樓轉換層頂面不平而未先修正，第一層模組就帶著傾斜，後續每層依前一層對位使傾斜延續到頂部，帷幕外牆接縫上寬下窄，只能在高樓層以異形板件收邊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An uneven podium transfer slab left uncorrected tilts the first module level, each later level aligns to the one below so the tilt continues to the roof, and façade joints widen toward the top, ending in special-shaped closure panels at high level. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此安裝時每隔幾層就要量測標高與垂直度並以墊片修正，裙樓或轉換層頂面的精度要求也必須比一般樓板嚴格。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Installation therefore measures level and verticality every few storeys and corrects with shims, and the top of the podium or transfer level needs tighter accuracy than an ordinary slab.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要每個模組都在製造公差內，堆疊後整棟建築也必然在公差內。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If every module is within its fabrication tolerance, the stacked building must be too.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"裙樓轉換層頂面不平而未先修正，第一層模組就帶著傾斜，後續每層依前一層對位使傾斜延續到頂部，帷幕外牆接縫上寬下窄，只能在高樓層以異形板件收邊。","textEn":"An uneven podium transfer slab left uncorrected tilts the first module level, each later level aligns to the one below so the tilt continues to the roof, and façade joints widen toward the top, ending in special-shaped closure panels at high level.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「堆疊公差、墊片與垂直度控制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stacking tolerances, shims and verticality control\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["裙樓轉換層頂面不平而未先修正，第一層模組就帶著傾斜，後續每層依前一層對位使傾斜延續到頂部，帷幕外牆接縫上寬下窄，只能在高樓層以異形板件收邊。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","模組在工廠製造，品質自然比工地好，不需要另外檢驗。"],"optionsEn":["An uneven podium transfer slab left uncorrected tilts the first module level, each later level aligns to the one below so the tilt continues to the roof, and façade joints widen toward the top, ending in special-shaped closure panels at high level.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Factory-made modules are naturally better than site work, so no separate inspection is needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"裙樓轉換層頂面不平而未先修正，第一層模組就帶著傾斜，後續每層依前一層對位使傾斜延續到頂部，帷幕外牆接縫上寬下窄，只能在高樓層以異形板件收邊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An uneven podium transfer slab left uncorrected tilts the first module level, each later level aligns to the one below so the tilt continues to the roof, and façade joints widen toward the top, ending in special-shaped closure panels at high level. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b100-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「工廠製造檢驗與尺寸驗收」與「現場接頭、防火封堵與防水檢查」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Factory inspection and dimensional acceptance\" and \"Site joints, fire stopping and waterproofing checks\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b100-v13-25","title":"工廠製造檢驗與尺寸驗收：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Factory inspection and dimensional acceptance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「出廠檢查表」如何影響建築模組化吊裝與接合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Factory release checklist” governs force, deformation or durability in “Volumetric modular-building lifting and connections”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"模組化的品質大部分在工廠決定：結構焊接、尺寸方正、防水層、防火封堵與機電管線都在出廠前完成，到工地後很難再打開檢查。因此工廠要建立與工地同等嚴格的檢驗制度，包含原物料證明、焊接檢查、尺寸量測、給排水試壓與電氣測試，並由第三方或主管機關在廠內查驗。ICC/MBI 1205 規範廠內與現場檢查及法規符合程序，新加坡則對 PPVC 製造廠實施認證制度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「出廠檢查表」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Most of a module's quality is decided in the factory: structural welds, dimensional squareness, waterproofing, fire stopping and services are all complete before shipping and hard to open up again on site. The factory therefore needs an inspection regime as strict as on site, covering material certificates, weld inspection, dimensional measurement, plumbing pressure tests and electrical tests, with in-plant inspection by third parties or the authority. ICC/MBI 1205 sets in-plant and on-site inspection and regulatory-compliance procedures, and Singapore runs an accreditation scheme for PPVC manufacturers. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Factory release checklist” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：3.6 m × 12.0 m 模組的理論對角線 √(3.6² + 12.0²) = √156.96 ≈ 12.528 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The theoretical diagonal of a 3.6 m × 12.0 m module is √(3.6² + 12.0²) = √156.96 ≈ 12.528 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「模組在工廠製造，品質自然比工地好，不需要另外檢驗。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Factory-made modules are naturally better than site work, so no separate inspection is needed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「出廠檢查表」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Factory release checklist”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-25-k1","title":"工廠製造檢驗與尺寸驗收","titleEn":"Factory inspection and dimensional acceptance","text":"模組化的品質大部分在工廠決定：結構焊接、尺寸方正、防水層、防火封堵與機電管線都在出廠前完成，到工地後很難再打開檢查。因此工廠要建立與工地同等嚴格的檢驗制度，包含原物料證明、焊接檢查、尺寸量測、給排水試壓與電氣測試，並由第三方或主管機關在廠內查驗。","textEn":"Most of a module's quality is decided in the factory: structural welds, dimensional squareness, waterproofing, fire stopping and services are all complete before shipping and hard to open up again on site. The factory therefore needs an inspection regime as strict as on site, covering material certificates, weld inspection, dimensional measurement, plumbing pressure tests and electrical tests, with in-plant inspection by third parties or the authority.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模組在工廠製造，品質自然比工地好，不需要另外檢驗。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Factory-made modules are naturally better than site work, so no separate inspection is needed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「工廠製造檢驗與尺寸驗收」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Factory inspection and dimensional acceptance\" is correct?","options":["模組在工廠製造，品質自然比工地好，不需要另外檢驗。","模組化的品質大部分在工廠決定：結構焊接、尺寸方正、防水層、防火封堵與機電管線都在出廠前完成，到工地後很難再打開檢查。","扳手鎖到規定扭矩，就代表螺栓預拉力一定正確。"],"optionsEn":["Factory-made modules are naturally better than site work, so no separate inspection is needed.","Most of a module's quality is decided in the factory: structural welds, dimensional squareness, waterproofing, fire stopping and services are all complete before shipping and hard to open up again on site.","Tightening to the specified torque guarantees the correct bolt preload."],"answer":1,"explanation":"模組化的品質大部分在工廠決定：結構焊接、尺寸方正、防水層、防火封堵與機電管線都在出廠前完成，到工地後很難再打開檢查。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Most of a module's quality is decided in the factory: structural welds, dimensional squareness, waterproofing, fire stopping and services are all complete before shipping and hard to open up again on site. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b100-v13-26","title":"工廠製造檢驗與尺寸驗收：定量估算","titleEn":"Factory inspection and dimensional acceptance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出廠檢查表」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Factory release checklist” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：3.6 m × 12.0 m 模組的理論對角線 √(3.6² + 12.0²) = √156.96 ≈ 12.528 m。實測兩對角線 12.531 m 與 12.522 m，差 9 mm，大於教學假設的允許差 6 mm，表示框架歪斜，須在出廠前調整，否則角部接頭到現場將無法對位。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The theoretical diagonal of a 3.6 m × 12.0 m module is √(3.6² + 12.0²) = √156.96 ≈ 12.528 m. Measured diagonals of 12.531 m and 12.522 m differ by 9 mm, more than an assumed allowable 6 mm, showing a racked frame that must be corrected before shipping or the corner joints will not align on site. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每個模組出廠前完成檢查表：對角線與高度量測、焊接目視與抽樣非破壞檢測、試水與試壓、電氣絕緣測試、防火封堵照片，由廠內品管與第三方簽名；檢查表與模組編號綁定，隨模組送到工地供驗收比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before shipping, complete a checklist for each module: diagonal and height measurements, visual and sampled non-destructive weld testing, water and pressure tests, electrical insulation tests and photographs of fire stopping, signed by factory QA and a third party; the checklist is tied to the module number and travels with it for comparison at site acceptance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"3.6 m × 12.0 m 模組的理論對角線 √(3.6² + 12.0²) = √156.96 ≈ 12.528 m。實測兩對角線 12.531 m 與 12.522 m，差 9 mm，大於教學假設的允許差 6 mm，表示框架歪斜，須在出廠前調整，否則角部接頭到現場將無法對位。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The theoretical diagonal of a 3.6 m × 12.0 m module is √(3.6² + 12.0²) = √156.96 ≈ 12.528 m. Measured diagonals of 12.531 m and 12.522 m differ by 9 mm, more than an assumed allowable 6 mm, showing a racked frame that must be corrected before shipping or the corner joints will not align on site. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「工廠製造檢驗與尺寸驗收」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Factory inspection and dimensional acceptance\", which statement holds?","options":["模組建築完工後就與一般建築相同，不需要保存模組層級的資料。","模組只要上下疊好，自重就足以讓建築維持整體性。","3.6 m × 12.0 m 模組的理論對角線 √(3.6² + 12.0²) = √156.96 ≈ 12.528 m。"],"optionsEn":["Once completed, a modular building is like any other and needs no module-level records.","As long as modules are stacked properly, self-weight alone keeps the building intact.","The theoretical diagonal of a 3.6 m × 12.0 m module is √(3.6² + 12.0²) = √156.96 ≈ 12.528 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"3.6 m × 12.0 m 模組的理論對角線 √(3.6² + 12.0²) = √156.96 ≈ 12.528 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The theoretical diagonal of a 3.6 m × 12.0 m module is √(3.6² + 12.0²) = √156.96 ≈ 12.528 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b100-v13-27","title":"工廠製造檢驗與尺寸驗收：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Factory inspection and dimensional acceptance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出廠檢查表」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Factory release checklist” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每個模組出廠前完成檢查表：對角線與高度量測、焊接目視與抽樣非破壞檢測、試水與試壓、電氣絕緣測試、防火封堵照片，由廠內品管與第三方簽名；檢查表與模組編號綁定，隨模組送到工地供驗收比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before shipping, complete a checklist for each module: diagonal and height measurements, visual and sampled non-destructive weld testing, water and pressure tests, electrical insulation tests and photographs of fire stopping, signed by factory QA and a third party; the checklist is tied to the module number and travels with it for comparison at site acceptance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：合約要求工廠品質計畫、檢查表樣式與第三方查驗頻率，並設出廠放行保留點：未完成檢查表與簽認的模組不得裝車；工地收貨時再以抽樣量測確認運輸未造成損傷。","observationEn":"Site practice: The contract should require a factory quality plan, checklist format and third-party inspection frequency, with a release hold point so no module without a completed, signed checklist is loaded; at site receipt, sample measurements confirm that transport caused no damage.","failure":"注意干擾：工廠為了趕交期而跳過試水與試壓，模組堆疊後才發現衛浴管線接頭滲漏，只能拆除已完成的裝修甚至吊出模組；尺寸歪斜的模組被勉強安裝，接頭只能在現場切割修改。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A factory that skips water and pressure tests to meet deadlines finds bathroom pipe joints leaking only after the modules are stacked, forcing removal of finished linings or even lifting modules back out; racked modules forced into place can only be connected by cutting joints on site. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每個模組出廠前完成檢查表：對角線與高度量測、焊接目視與抽樣非破壞檢測、試水與試壓、電氣絕緣測試、防火封堵照片，由廠內品管與第三方簽名；檢查表與模組編號綁定，隨模組送到工地供驗收比對。","textEn":"Before shipping, complete a checklist for each module: diagonal and height measurements, visual and sampled non-destructive weld testing, water and pressure tests, electrical insulation tests and photographs of fire stopping, signed by factory QA and a third party; the checklist is tied to the module number and travels with it for comparison at site acceptance.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"合約要求工廠品質計畫、檢查表樣式與第三方查驗頻率，並設出廠放行保留點：未完成檢查表與簽認的模組不得裝車；工地收貨時再以抽樣量測確認運輸未造成損傷。","textEn":"The contract should require a factory quality plan, checklist format and third-party inspection frequency, with a release hold point so no module without a completed, signed checklist is loaded; at site receipt, sample measurements confirm that transport caused no damage.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「工廠製造檢驗與尺寸驗收」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Factory inspection and dimensional acceptance\"?","options":["每個模組出廠前完成檢查表：對角線與高度量測、焊接目視與抽樣非破壞檢測、試水與試壓、電氣絕緣測試、防火封堵照片，由廠內品管與第三方簽名。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","模組既然能承受使用荷載，用任何方式吊起來都不會受損。"],"optionsEn":["Before shipping, complete a checklist for each module: diagonal and height measurements, visual and sampled non-destructive weld testing, water and pressure tests, electrical insulation tests and photographs of fire stopping, signed by factory QA and a third party.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Since a module can carry service loads, any way of lifting it will do no harm."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每個模組出廠前完成檢查表：對角線與高度量測、焊接目視與抽樣非破壞檢測、試水與試壓、電氣絕緣測試、防火封堵照片，由廠內品管與第三方簽名；檢查表與模組編號綁定，隨模組送到工地供驗收比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before shipping, complete a checklist for each module: diagonal and height measurements, visual and sampled non-destructive weld testing, water and pressure tests, electrical insulation tests and photographs of fire stopping, signed by factory QA and a third party; the checklist is tied to the module number and travels with it for comparison at site acceptance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b100-v13-28","title":"工廠製造檢驗與尺寸驗收：失效診斷","titleEn":"Factory inspection and dimensional acceptance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出廠檢查表」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Factory release checklist” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"工廠為了趕交期而跳過試水與試壓，模組堆疊後才發現衛浴管線接頭滲漏，只能拆除已完成的裝修甚至吊出模組；尺寸歪斜的模組被勉強安裝，接頭只能在現場切割修改。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A factory that skips water and pressure tests to meet deadlines finds bathroom pipe joints leaking only after the modules are stacked, forcing removal of finished linings or even lifting modules back out; racked modules forced into place can only be connected by cutting joints on site. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：ICC/MBI 1205 規範廠內與現場檢查及法規符合程序，新加坡則對 PPVC 製造廠實施認證制度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: ICC/MBI 1205 sets in-plant and on-site inspection and regulatory-compliance procedures, and Singapore runs an accreditation scheme for PPVC manufacturers.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模組在工廠製造，品質自然比工地好，不需要另外檢驗。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Factory-made modules are naturally better than site work, so no separate inspection is needed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"工廠為了趕交期而跳過試水與試壓，模組堆疊後才發現衛浴管線接頭滲漏，只能拆除已完成的裝修甚至吊出模組；尺寸歪斜的模組被勉強安裝，接頭只能在現場切割修改。","textEn":"A factory that skips water and pressure tests to meet deadlines finds bathroom pipe joints leaking only after the modules are stacked, forcing removal of finished linings or even lifting modules back out; racked modules forced into place can only be connected by cutting joints on site.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「工廠製造檢驗與尺寸驗收」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Factory inspection and dimensional acceptance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","工廠為了趕交期而跳過試水與試壓，模組堆疊後才發現衛浴管線接頭滲漏，只能拆除已完成的裝修甚至吊出模組；尺寸歪斜的模組被勉強安裝，接頭只能在現場切割修改。","扳手鎖到規定扭矩，就代表螺栓預拉力一定正確。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A factory that skips water and pressure tests to meet deadlines finds bathroom pipe joints leaking only after the modules are stacked, forcing removal of finished linings or even lifting modules back out.","Tightening to the specified torque guarantees the correct bolt preload."],"answer":1,"explanation":"工廠為了趕交期而跳過試水與試壓，模組堆疊後才發現衛浴管線接頭滲漏，只能拆除已完成的裝修甚至吊出模組；尺寸歪斜的模組被勉強安裝，接頭只能在現場切割修改。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A factory that skips water and pressure tests to meet deadlines finds bathroom pipe joints leaking only after the modules are stacked, forcing removal of finished linings or even lifting modules back out; racked modules forced into place can only be connected by cutting joints on site. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b100-v13-29","title":"現場接頭、防火封堵與防水檢查：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Site joints, fire stopping and waterproofing checks: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「螺栓預拉力與封堵檢查」如何影響建築模組化吊裝與接合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bolt preload and sealing checks” governs force, deformation or durability in “Volumetric modular-building lifting and connections”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"模組落位後還有一連串現場工作決定成敗：螺栓鎖固與檢查、灌漿或現場焊接、模組間防水接縫、屋頂與外牆的臨時防護，以及模組之間的防火封堵與隔音。這些位置多半在吊裝後很快被下一個模組遮住，所以必須跟著吊裝節奏逐層檢查。螺栓預拉力透過扭矩係數與鎖固扭矩相關，而扭矩係數會隨表面狀況改變，重要接頭宜以校正過的工具配合轉角法等方式確認。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「螺栓預拉力與封堵檢查」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After a module is set, a chain of site work decides success: bolt tightening and checks, grouting or site welding, waterproof joints between modules, temporary protection of roof and façade, and fire stopping and acoustic sealing between modules. Most of these locations are soon hidden by the next module, so they must be inspected level by level at the pace of lifting. Bolt preload depends on tightening torque through a torque coefficient that varies with surface condition, so critical joints should be confirmed with calibrated tools and methods such as turn-of-nut. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Bolt preload and sealing checks” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：預拉力 F_p = 0.7·f_ub·A_s = 0.7×800×245 ≈ 137.2 kN（8.8 級 M20）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Preload F_p = 0.7·f_ub·A_s = 0.7×800×245 ≈ 137.2 kN for an M20 grade 8.8 bolt.","failure":"常見誤解：「扳手鎖到規定扭矩，就代表螺栓預拉力一定正確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Tightening to the specified torque guarantees the correct bolt preload.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「螺栓預拉力與封堵檢查」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Bolt preload and sealing checks”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-29-k1","title":"現場接頭、防火封堵與防水檢查","titleEn":"Site joints, fire stopping and waterproofing checks","text":"模組落位後還有一連串現場工作決定成敗：螺栓鎖固與檢查、灌漿或現場焊接、模組間防水接縫、屋頂與外牆的臨時防護，以及模組之間的防火封堵與隔音。這些位置多半在吊裝後很快被下一個模組遮住，所以必須跟著吊裝節奏逐層檢查。","textEn":"After a module is set, a chain of site work decides success: bolt tightening and checks, grouting or site welding, waterproof joints between modules, temporary protection of roof and façade, and fire stopping and acoustic sealing between modules. Most of these locations are soon hidden by the next module, so they must be inspected level by level at the pace of lifting.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：扳手鎖到規定扭矩，就代表螺栓預拉力一定正確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Tightening to the specified torque guarantees the correct bolt preload. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「現場接頭、防火封堵與防水檢查」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Site joints, fire stopping and waterproofing checks\" is correct?","options":["扳手鎖到規定扭矩，就代表螺栓預拉力一定正確。","模組在工廠已做好防水，現場吊裝期間不需要另外防雨。","模組落位後還有一連串現場工作決定成敗：螺栓鎖固與檢查、灌漿或現場焊接、模組間防水接縫、屋頂與外牆的臨時防護，以及模組之間的防火封堵與隔音。"],"optionsEn":["Tightening to the specified torque guarantees the correct bolt preload.","Modules are waterproofed in the factory, so no rain protection is needed during site installation.","After a module is set, a chain of site work decides success: bolt tightening and checks, grouting or site welding, waterproof joints between modules, temporary protection of roof and façade, and fire stopping and acoustic sealing between modules."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模組落位後還有一連串現場工作決定成敗：螺栓鎖固與檢查、灌漿或現場焊接、模組間防水接縫、屋頂與外牆的臨時防護，以及模組之間的防火封堵與隔音。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After a module is set, a chain of site work decides success: bolt tightening and checks, grouting or site welding, waterproof joints between modules, temporary protection of roof and façade, and fire stopping and acoustic sealing between modules. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b100-v13-30","title":"現場接頭、防火封堵與防水檢查：定量估算","titleEn":"Site joints, fire stopping and waterproofing checks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「螺栓預拉力與封堵檢查」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bolt preload and sealing checks” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：預拉力 F_p = 0.7·f_ub·A_s = 0.7×800×245 ≈ 137.2 kN（8.8 級 M20）。以 T = K·F·d 估算扭矩，K = 0.20、d = 0.020 m：T = 0.20×137,200×0.020 ≈ 549 N·m；若潤滑使 K 降為 0.14，同樣扭矩會產生約 137.2×0.20/0.14 ≈ 196 kN，可能超出螺栓降伏。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Preload F_p = 0.7·f_ub·A_s = 0.7×800×245 ≈ 137.2 kN for an M20 grade 8.8 bolt. Estimating torque by T = K·F·d with K = 0.20 and d = 0.020 m gives T = 0.20×137,200×0.020 ≈ 549 N·m; if lubrication lowers K to 0.14, the same torque produces about 137.2×0.20/0.14 ≈ 196 kN, possibly beyond bolt yield. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每層吊裝後由檢查員確認螺栓數量、鎖固標記與抽樣扭矩，灌漿接頭檢查灌漿紀錄；在下一個模組覆蓋前拍照記錄防火封堵與防水接縫，並對外牆接縫做試水，紀錄與模組編號連結。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After each level is lifted, an inspector confirms bolt count, tightening marks and sampled torque, and checks grout records for grouted joints; before the next module covers them, fire stopping and waterproof joints are photographed, façade joints are water-tested, and records are linked to module numbers.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"預拉力 F_p = 0.7·f_ub·A_s = 0.7×800×245 ≈ 137.2 kN（8.8 級 M20）。以 T = K·F·d 估算扭矩，K = 0.20、d = 0.020 m：T = 0.20×137,200×0.020 ≈ 549 N·m；若潤滑使 K 降為 0.14，同樣扭矩會產生約 137.2×0.20/0.14 ≈ 196 kN，可能超出螺栓降伏。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Preload F_p = 0.7·f_ub·A_s = 0.7×800×245 ≈ 137.2 kN for an M20 grade 8.8 bolt. Estimating torque by T = K·F·d with K = 0.20 and d = 0.020 m gives T = 0.20×137,200×0.020 ≈ 549 N·m; if lubrication lowers K to 0.14, the same torque produces about 137.2×0.20/0.14 ≈ 196 kN, possibly beyond bolt yield. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「現場接頭、防火封堵與防水檢查」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Site joints, fire stopping and waterproofing checks\", which statement holds?","options":["預拉力 F_p = 0.7·f_ub·A_s = 0.7×800×245 ≈ 137.2 kN（8.8 級 M20）。","模組在工廠已經做好結構，堆疊後不需要整體結構分析。","模組接頭只要強度計算通過，安裝方式可以留給現場決定。"],"optionsEn":["Preload F_p = 0.7·f_ub·A_s = 0.7×800×245 ≈ 137.2 kN for an M20 grade 8.8 bolt.","Since each module's structure is finished in the factory, the stacked building needs no overall structural analysis.","Once a module joint passes the strength calculation, how it is installed can be left to the site."],"answer":0,"explanation":"預拉力 F_p = 0.7·f_ub·A_s = 0.7×800×245 ≈ 137.2 kN（8.8 級 M20）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Preload F_p = 0.7·f_ub·A_s = 0.7×800×245 ≈ 137.2 kN for an M20 grade 8.8 bolt. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b100-v13-31","title":"現場接頭、防火封堵與防水檢查：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Site joints, fire stopping and waterproofing checks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「螺栓預拉力與封堵檢查」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bolt preload and sealing checks” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每層吊裝後由檢查員確認螺栓數量、鎖固標記與抽樣扭矩，灌漿接頭檢查灌漿紀錄；在下一個模組覆蓋前拍照記錄防火封堵與防水接縫，並對外牆接縫做試水，紀錄與模組編號連結。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After each level is lifted, an inspector confirms bolt count, tightening marks and sampled torque, and checks grout records for grouted joints; before the next module covers them, fire stopping and waterproof joints are photographed, façade joints are water-tested, and records are linked to module numbers. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把接頭檢查、防火封堵與防水接縫列為每一層的保留點，未經檢查員簽認不得吊放覆蓋該處的模組；扭矩工具定期校正，並先在工地以預拉力試驗確認扭矩係數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Make joint checks, fire stopping and waterproof joints a hold point at every level, with no covering module lifted until the inspector signs off; calibrate torque tools regularly and confirm the torque coefficient on site with preload tests first.","failure":"注意干擾：為趕吊裝進度讓下一個模組先覆蓋，未檢查的接頭從此無法進入；防火封堵遺漏使模組間空腔連通多個樓層，日後火災時煙與火沿空腔蔓延。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Rushing the lifting sequence so the next module covers joints before inspection leaves them permanently inaccessible; missing fire stopping links inter-module cavities through several floors so that in a later fire smoke and flame travel along the cavities. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每層吊裝後由檢查員確認螺栓數量、鎖固標記與抽樣扭矩，灌漿接頭檢查灌漿紀錄；在下一個模組覆蓋前拍照記錄防火封堵與防水接縫，並對外牆接縫做試水，紀錄與模組編號連結。","textEn":"After each level is lifted, an inspector confirms bolt count, tightening marks and sampled torque, and checks grout records for grouted joints; before the next module covers them, fire stopping and waterproof joints are photographed, façade joints are water-tested, and records are linked to module numbers.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把接頭檢查、防火封堵與防水接縫列為每一層的保留點，未經檢查員簽認不得吊放覆蓋該處的模組；扭矩工具定期校正，並先在工地以預拉力試驗確認扭矩係數。","textEn":"Make joint checks, fire stopping and waterproof joints a hold point at every level, with no covering module lifted until the inspector signs off; calibrate torque tools regularly and confirm the torque coefficient on site with preload tests first.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「現場接頭、防火封堵與防水檢查」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Site joints, fire stopping and waterproofing checks\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","每層吊裝後由檢查員確認螺栓數量、鎖固標記與抽樣扭矩，灌漿接頭檢查灌漿紀錄；在下一個模組覆蓋前拍照記錄防火封堵與防水接縫，並對外牆接縫做試水，紀錄與模組編號連結。","只要起重機額定荷重夠大，任何風速都可以吊模組。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","After each level is lifted, an inspector confirms bolt count, tightening marks and sampled torque, and checks grout records for grouted joints.","If the crane's rated capacity is large enough, modules can be lifted at any wind speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每層吊裝後由檢查員確認螺栓數量、鎖固標記與抽樣扭矩，灌漿接頭檢查灌漿紀錄；在下一個模組覆蓋前拍照記錄防火封堵與防水接縫，並對外牆接縫做試水，紀錄與模組編號連結。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After each level is lifted, an inspector confirms bolt count, tightening marks and sampled torque, and checks grout records for grouted joints; before the next module covers them, fire stopping and waterproof joints are photographed, façade joints are water-tested, and records are linked to module numbers. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b100-v13-32","title":"現場接頭、防火封堵與防水檢查：失效診斷","titleEn":"Site joints, fire stopping and waterproofing checks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「螺栓預拉力與封堵檢查」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bolt preload and sealing checks” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為趕吊裝進度讓下一個模組先覆蓋，未檢查的接頭從此無法進入；防火封堵遺漏使模組間空腔連通多個樓層，日後火災時煙與火沿空腔蔓延。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Rushing the lifting sequence so the next module covers joints before inspection leaves them permanently inaccessible; missing fire stopping links inter-module cavities through several floors so that in a later fire smoke and flame travel along the cavities. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：螺栓預拉力透過扭矩係數與鎖固扭矩相關，而扭矩係數會隨表面狀況改變，重要接頭宜以校正過的工具配合轉角法等方式確認。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Bolt preload depends on tightening torque through a torque coefficient that varies with surface condition, so critical joints should be confirmed with calibrated tools and methods such as turn-of-nut.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「扳手鎖到規定扭矩，就代表螺栓預拉力一定正確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Tightening to the specified torque guarantees the correct bolt preload.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為趕吊裝進度讓下一個模組先覆蓋，未檢查的接頭從此無法進入；防火封堵遺漏使模組間空腔連通多個樓層，日後火災時煙與火沿空腔蔓延。","textEn":"Rushing the lifting sequence so the next module covers joints before inspection leaves them permanently inaccessible; missing fire stopping links inter-module cavities through several floors so that in a later fire smoke and flame travel along the cavities.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「現場接頭、防火封堵與防水檢查」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Site joints, fire stopping and waterproofing checks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","模組在工廠已做好防水，現場吊裝期間不需要另外防雨。","為趕吊裝進度讓下一個模組先覆蓋，未檢查的接頭從此無法進入；防火封堵遺漏使模組間空腔連通多個樓層，日後火災時煙與火沿空腔蔓延。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Modules are waterproofed in the factory, so no rain protection is needed during site installation.","Rushing the lifting sequence so the next module covers joints before inspection leaves them permanently inaccessible."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為趕吊裝進度讓下一個模組先覆蓋，未檢查的接頭從此無法進入；防火封堵遺漏使模組間空腔連通多個樓層，日後火災時煙與火沿空腔蔓延。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Rushing the lifting sequence so the next module covers joints before inspection leaves them permanently inaccessible; missing fire stopping links inter-module cavities through several floors so that in a later fire smoke and flame travel along the cavities. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b100-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「模組間空腔的防火、防潮與耐久」與「模組履歷、維修更換與交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fire, moisture and durability of inter-module cavities\" and \"Module records, repair and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b100-v13-33","title":"模組間空腔的防火、防潮與耐久：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Fire, moisture and durability of inter-module cavities: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「模組間空腔」如何影響建築模組化吊裝與接合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Inter-module cavities” governs force, deformation or durability in “Volumetric modular-building lifting and connections”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"模組建築的雙層牆與雙層樓板之間形成許多隱藏空腔，它們讓模組能獨立製造，卻也帶來耐久與防火風險：施工期間未覆蓋的模組頂部遇雨，水會流入空腔與隔熱材中久久不乾；空腔若沒有分隔，火煙可沿著它跨越樓層；鋼接頭藏在空腔內，長期潮濕會鏽蝕卻難以檢查。因此設計要提供空腔分隔、排水與通風路徑，並規劃日後的檢查開口。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「模組間空腔」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The double walls and floors of modular buildings create many concealed cavities that allow modules to be made independently but bring durability and fire risks: rain on uncovered module tops during construction runs into cavities and insulation and stays wet for a long time, unsubdivided cavities let fire and smoke cross floors, and steel joints hidden inside can corrode in long-term damp while being hard to inspect. The design must therefore provide cavity barriers, drainage and ventilation paths and plan inspection openings for later. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Inter-module cavities” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：一個 3.6 m × 12 m 模組頂面 43.2 m²，若未覆蓋時遇到 50 mm 降雨，落在頂面的雨水約 43.2×0.05 = 2.16 m³，即約 2,160 L；只要其中一成滲入空腔，就有約 216 L 的水進入隔熱材與石膏板。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The 43.2 m² top of a 3.6 m × 12 m module left uncovered in a 50 mm rainfall receives about 43.2×0.05 = 2.16 m³, roughly 2,160 L; if only a tenth enters the cavities, about 216 L of water reaches the insulation and plasterboard.","failure":"常見誤解：「模組在工廠已做好防水，現場吊裝期間不需要另外防雨。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Modules are waterproofed in the factory, so no rain protection is needed during site installation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「模組間空腔」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Inter-module cavities”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-33-k1","title":"模組間空腔的防火、防潮與耐久","titleEn":"Fire, moisture and durability of inter-module cavities","text":"模組建築的雙層牆與雙層樓板之間形成許多隱藏空腔，它們讓模組能獨立製造，卻也帶來耐久與防火風險：施工期間未覆蓋的模組頂部遇雨，水會流入空腔與隔熱材中久久不乾；空腔若沒有分隔，火煙可沿著它跨越樓層；鋼接頭藏在空腔內，長期潮濕會鏽蝕卻難以檢查。因此設計要提供空腔分隔、排水與通風路徑，並規劃日後的檢查開口。","textEn":"The double walls and floors of modular buildings create many concealed cavities that allow modules to be made independently but bring durability and fire risks: rain on uncovered module tops during construction runs into cavities and insulation and stays wet for a long time, unsubdivided cavities let fire and smoke cross floors, and steel joints hidden inside can corrode in long-term damp while being hard to inspect. The design must therefore provide cavity barriers, drainage and ventilation paths and plan inspection openings for later.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模組在工廠已做好防水，現場吊裝期間不需要另外防雨。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Modules are waterproofed in the factory, so no rain protection is needed during site installation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模組間空腔的防火、防潮與耐久」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fire, moisture and durability of inter-module cavities\" is correct?","options":["模組建築的雙層牆與雙層樓板之間形成許多隱藏空腔，它們讓模組能獨立製造，卻也帶來耐久與防火風險：施工期間未覆蓋的模組頂部遇雨，水會流入空腔與隔熱材中久久不乾。","模組在工廠已做好防水，現場吊裝期間不需要另外防雨。","模組建築完工後就與一般建築相同，不需要保存模組層級的資料。"],"optionsEn":["The double walls and floors of modular buildings create many concealed cavities that allow modules to be made independently but bring durability and fire risks: rain on uncovered module tops during construction runs into cavities and insulation and stays wet for a long time, unsubdivided cavities let fire and smoke cross floors, and steel joints hidden inside can corrode in long-term damp while being hard to inspect.","Modules are waterproofed in the factory, so no rain protection is needed during site installation.","Once completed, a modular building is like any other and needs no module-level records."],"answer":0,"explanation":"模組建築的雙層牆與雙層樓板之間形成許多隱藏空腔，它們讓模組能獨立製造，卻也帶來耐久與防火風險：施工期間未覆蓋的模組頂部遇雨，水會流入空腔與隔熱材中久久不乾；空腔若沒有分隔，火煙可沿著它跨越樓層；鋼接頭藏在空腔內，長期潮濕會鏽蝕卻難以檢查。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The double walls and floors of modular buildings create many concealed cavities that allow modules to be made independently but bring durability and fire risks: rain on uncovered module tops during construction runs into cavities and insulation and stays wet for a long time, unsubdivided cavities let fire and smoke cross floors, and steel joints hidden inside can corrode in long-term damp while being hard to inspect. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b100-v13-34","title":"模組間空腔的防火、防潮與耐久：定量估算","titleEn":"Fire, moisture and durability of inter-module cavities: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模組間空腔」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Inter-module cavities” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：一個 3.6 m × 12 m 模組頂面 43.2 m²，若未覆蓋時遇到 50 mm 降雨，落在頂面的雨水約 43.2×0.05 = 2.16 m³，即約 2,160 L；只要其中一成滲入空腔，就有約 216 L 的水進入隔熱材與石膏板。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The 43.2 m² top of a 3.6 m × 12 m module left uncovered in a 50 mm rainfall receives about 43.2×0.05 = 2.16 m³, roughly 2,160 L; if only a tenth enters the cavities, about 216 L of water reaches the insulation and plasterboard. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：安裝期間每天收工前檢查模組頂部的臨時防水覆蓋，雨後以含水率計抽查空腔內木料、石膏板與隔熱材；完工前確認空腔分隔完整，並以內視鏡或預留開口抽查鋼接頭的防蝕狀況。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: During installation inspect temporary waterproof covers on module tops before the end of each shift, spot-check moisture content of timber, plasterboard and insulation in cavities with a moisture meter after rain, and before completion confirm cavity barriers are complete and check corrosion protection of steel joints through borescopes or planned openings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"一個 3.6 m × 12 m 模組頂面 43.2 m²，若未覆蓋時遇到 50 mm 降雨，落在頂面的雨水約 43.2×0.05 = 2.16 m³，即約 2,160 L；只要其中一成滲入空腔，就有約 216 L 的水進入隔熱材與石膏板。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The 43.2 m² top of a 3.6 m × 12 m module left uncovered in a 50 mm rainfall receives about 43.2×0.05 = 2.16 m³, roughly 2,160 L; if only a tenth enters the cavities, about 216 L of water reaches the insulation and plasterboard. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模組間空腔的防火、防潮與耐久」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fire, moisture and durability of inter-module cavities\", which statement holds?","options":["模組只要上下疊好，自重就足以讓建築維持整體性。","一個 3.6 m × 12 m 模組頂面 43.2 m²，若未覆蓋時遇到 50 mm 降雨，落在頂面的雨水約 43.2×0.05 = 2.16 m³，即約 2,160 L。","模組既然能承受使用荷載，用任何方式吊起來都不會受損。"],"optionsEn":["As long as modules are stacked properly, self-weight alone keeps the building intact.","The 43.2 m² top of a 3.6 m × 12 m module left uncovered in a 50 mm rainfall receives about 43.2×0.05 = 2.16 m³, roughly 2,160 L.","Since a module can carry service loads, any way of lifting it will do no harm."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一個 3.6 m × 12 m 模組頂面 43.2 m²，若未覆蓋時遇到 50 mm 降雨，落在頂面的雨水約 43.2×0.05 = 2.16 m³，即約 2,160 L；只要其中一成滲入空腔，就有約 216 L 的水進入隔熱材與石膏板。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The 43.2 m² top of a 3.6 m × 12 m module left uncovered in a 50 mm rainfall receives about 43.2×0.05 = 2.16 m³, roughly 2,160 L; if only a tenth enters the cavities, about 216 L of water reaches the insulation and plasterboard. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b100-v13-35","title":"模組間空腔的防火、防潮與耐久：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fire, moisture and durability of inter-module cavities: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模組間空腔」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Inter-module cavities” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"安裝期間每天收工前檢查模組頂部的臨時防水覆蓋，雨後以含水率計抽查空腔內木料、石膏板與隔熱材；完工前確認空腔分隔完整，並以內視鏡或預留開口抽查鋼接頭的防蝕狀況。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"During installation inspect temporary waterproof covers on module tops before the end of each shift, spot-check moisture content of timber, plasterboard and insulation in cavities with a moisture meter after rain, and before completion confirm cavity barriers are complete and check corrosion protection of steel joints through borescopes or planned openings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工計畫要規定每一層吊裝完成後的臨時防水程序與責任人，雨後含水率超過門檻的模組須乾燥並經檢查員確認才能封閉；空腔分隔位置要在圖面與現場標示，並列入消防查驗項目。","observationEn":"Site practice: The construction plan must set the temporary waterproofing procedure and responsible person after each level is lifted; modules whose moisture content exceeds the threshold after rain must be dried and cleared by the inspector before closing, and cavity-barrier locations must be marked on drawings and on site and included in fire inspections.","failure":"注意干擾：施工中臨時防水覆蓋不足，雨水滲入多層模組的空腔，完工後出現發霉、地板變形與異味，只能拆開大量內裝乾燥與更換；空腔分隔遺漏時，火災中的煙可在住戶察覺前擴散到其他樓層。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Inadequate temporary weather protection lets rain into cavities across several module levels, and after completion mould, buckled floors and odours appear, requiring extensive linings to be opened, dried and replaced; missing cavity barriers let smoke from a fire spread to other floors before occupants notice. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"安裝期間每天收工前檢查模組頂部的臨時防水覆蓋，雨後以含水率計抽查空腔內木料、石膏板與隔熱材；完工前確認空腔分隔完整，並以內視鏡或預留開口抽查鋼接頭的防蝕狀況。","textEn":"During installation inspect temporary waterproof covers on module tops before the end of each shift, spot-check moisture content of timber, plasterboard and insulation in cavities with a moisture meter after rain, and before completion confirm cavity barriers are complete and check corrosion protection of steel joints through borescopes or planned openings.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工計畫要規定每一層吊裝完成後的臨時防水程序與責任人，雨後含水率超過門檻的模組須乾燥並經檢查員確認才能封閉；空腔分隔位置要在圖面與現場標示，並列入消防查驗項目。","textEn":"The construction plan must set the temporary waterproofing procedure and responsible person after each level is lifted; modules whose moisture content exceeds the threshold after rain must be dried and cleared by the inspector before closing, and cavity-barrier locations must be marked on drawings and on site and included in fire inspections.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模組間空腔的防火、防潮與耐久」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fire, moisture and durability of inter-module cavities\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要每個模組都在製造公差內，堆疊後整棟建築也必然在公差內。","安裝期間每天收工前檢查模組頂部的臨時防水覆蓋，雨後以含水率計抽查空腔內木料、石膏板與隔熱材；完工前確認空腔分隔完整，並以內視鏡或預留開口抽查鋼接頭的防蝕狀況。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","If every module is within its fabrication tolerance, the stacked building must be too.","During installation inspect temporary waterproof covers on module tops before the end of each shift, spot-check moisture content of timber, plasterboard and insulation in cavities with a moisture meter after rain, and before completion confirm cavity barriers are complete and check corrosion protection of steel joints through borescopes or planned openings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"安裝期間每天收工前檢查模組頂部的臨時防水覆蓋，雨後以含水率計抽查空腔內木料、石膏板與隔熱材；完工前確認空腔分隔完整，並以內視鏡或預留開口抽查鋼接頭的防蝕狀況。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"During installation inspect temporary waterproof covers on module tops before the end of each shift, spot-check moisture content of timber, plasterboard and insulation in cavities with a moisture meter after rain, and before completion confirm cavity barriers are complete and check corrosion protection of steel joints through borescopes or planned openings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b100-v13-36","title":"模組間空腔的防火、防潮與耐久：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fire, moisture and durability of inter-module cavities: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模組間空腔」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Inter-module cavities” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"施工中臨時防水覆蓋不足，雨水滲入多層模組的空腔，完工後出現發霉、地板變形與異味，只能拆開大量內裝乾燥與更換；空腔分隔遺漏時，火災中的煙可在住戶察覺前擴散到其他樓層。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Inadequate temporary weather protection lets rain into cavities across several module levels, and after completion mould, buckled floors and odours appear, requiring extensive linings to be opened, dried and replaced; missing cavity barriers let smoke from a fire spread to other floors before occupants notice. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此設計要提供空腔分隔、排水與通風路徑，並規劃日後的檢查開口。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The design must therefore provide cavity barriers, drainage and ventilation paths and plan inspection openings for later.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模組在工廠已做好防水，現場吊裝期間不需要另外防雨。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Modules are waterproofed in the factory, so no rain protection is needed during site installation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"施工中臨時防水覆蓋不足，雨水滲入多層模組的空腔，完工後出現發霉、地板變形與異味，只能拆開大量內裝乾燥與更換；空腔分隔遺漏時，火災中的煙可在住戶察覺前擴散到其他樓層。","textEn":"Inadequate temporary weather protection lets rain into cavities across several module levels, and after completion mould, buckled floors and odours appear, requiring extensive linings to be opened, dried and replaced; missing cavity barriers let smoke from a fire spread to other floors before occupants notice.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模組間空腔的防火、防潮與耐久」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fire, moisture and durability of inter-module cavities\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["施工中臨時防水覆蓋不足，雨水滲入多層模組的空腔，完工後出現發霉、地板變形與異味，只能拆開大量內裝乾燥與更換。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","模組建築完工後就與一般建築相同，不需要保存模組層級的資料。"],"optionsEn":["Inadequate temporary weather protection lets rain into cavities across several module levels, and after completion mould, buckled floors and odours appear, requiring extensive linings to be opened, dried and replaced.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Once completed, a modular building is like any other and needs no module-level records."],"answer":0,"explanation":"施工中臨時防水覆蓋不足，雨水滲入多層模組的空腔，完工後出現發霉、地板變形與異味，只能拆開大量內裝乾燥與更換；空腔分隔遺漏時，火災中的煙可在住戶察覺前擴散到其他樓層。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Inadequate temporary weather protection lets rain into cavities across several module levels, and after completion mould, buckled floors and odours appear, requiring extensive linings to be opened, dried and replaced; missing cavity barriers let smoke from a fire spread to other floors before occupants notice. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b100-v13-37","title":"模組履歷、維修更換與交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Module records, repair and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「模組履歷」如何影響建築模組化吊裝與接合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Module records” governs force, deformation or durability in “Volumetric modular-building lifting and connections”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"模組建築的每個箱體都是可追溯的產品：材料批號、焊接與試驗紀錄、安裝位置、墊片厚度與接頭檢查都應與模組編號連結。日後改裝時，住戶或設計者必須知道哪些牆是承重框架、哪些是可拆隔間、接頭位在哪裡；若需要修理或更換某個模組，也要知道它的連接方式與吊出路徑。把這些紀錄連到資產資訊模型交給業主，才能讓工廠品質延續到營運期。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「模組履歷」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each box in a modular building is a traceable product: material batches, welding and test records, installed location, shim thickness and joint inspections should all be linked to the module number. In later alterations occupants and designers must know which walls are structural frame, which are removable partitions and where the joints are; if a module must be repaired or replaced, its connections and lift-out route must also be known. Linking these records to the asset information model at handover is what carries the factory's quality into operation. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Module records” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以 1,866 個模組、每個模組約 30 個品質檢查點估算，共 1,866×30 = 55,980 筆紀錄；若不符合率 0.5%，約有 280 筆需追蹤處置與結案。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With 1,866 modules and about 30 quality checkpoints per module there are 1,866×30 = 55,980 records; at a 0.5% nonconformance rate about 280 items need tracking and close-out.","failure":"常見誤解：「模組建築完工後就與一般建築相同，不需要保存模組層級的資料。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once completed, a modular building is like any other and needs no module-level records.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「模組履歷」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Module records”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-37-k1","title":"模組履歷、維修更換與交接","titleEn":"Module records, repair and handover","text":"模組建築的每個箱體都是可追溯的產品：材料批號、焊接與試驗紀錄、安裝位置、墊片厚度與接頭檢查都應與模組編號連結。日後改裝時，住戶或設計者必須知道哪些牆是承重框架、哪些是可拆隔間、接頭位在哪裡；若需要修理或更換某個模組，也要知道它的連接方式與吊出路徑。","textEn":"Each box in a modular building is a traceable product: material batches, welding and test records, installed location, shim thickness and joint inspections should all be linked to the module number. In later alterations occupants and designers must know which walls are structural frame, which are removable partitions and where the joints are; if a module must be repaired or replaced, its connections and lift-out route must also be known.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模組建築完工後就與一般建築相同，不需要保存模組層級的資料。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once completed, a modular building is like any other and needs no module-level records. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模組履歷、維修更換與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Module records, repair and handover\" is correct?","options":["模組建築完工後就與一般建築相同，不需要保存模組層級的資料。","模組建築的每個箱體都是可追溯的產品：材料批號、焊接與試驗紀錄、安裝位置、墊片厚度與接頭檢查都應與模組編號連結。","模組在工廠已經做好結構，堆疊後不需要整體結構分析。"],"optionsEn":["Once completed, a modular building is like any other and needs no module-level records.","Each box in a modular building is a traceable product: material batches, welding and test records, installed location, shim thickness and joint inspections should all be linked to the module number.","Since each module's structure is finished in the factory, the stacked building needs no overall structural analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"模組建築的每個箱體都是可追溯的產品：材料批號、焊接與試驗紀錄、安裝位置、墊片厚度與接頭檢查都應與模組編號連結。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each box in a modular building is a traceable product: material batches, welding and test records, installed location, shim thickness and joint inspections should all be linked to the module number. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b100-v13-38","title":"模組履歷、維修更換與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Module records, repair and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模組履歷」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Module records” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以 1,866 個模組、每個模組約 30 個品質檢查點估算，共 1,866×30 = 55,980 筆紀錄；若不符合率 0.5%，約有 280 筆需追蹤處置與結案。模組數取自公開案例，檢查點數與不符合率為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With 1,866 modules and about 30 quality checkpoints per module there are 1,866×30 = 55,980 records; at a 0.5% nonconformance rate about 280 items need tracking and close-out. The module count comes from a public case; checkpoints and nonconformance rate are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：交接前抽查模組編號、位置與紀錄是否一致，確認所有不符合事項已結案；交接文件應包含模組配置圖、承重構件標示、接頭詳圖與檢查紀錄、維護與改裝限制，並由業主的設施管理單位確認可查詢。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before handover, spot-check that module numbers, positions and records agree and that every nonconformance is closed; the handover set should include the module layout, identification of structural elements, joint details and inspection records, and maintenance and alteration limits, confirmed as searchable by the owner's facilities team.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以 1,866 個模組、每個模組約 30 個品質檢查點估算，共 1,866×30 = 55,980 筆紀錄；若不符合率 0.5%，約有 280 筆需追蹤處置與結案。模組數取自公開案例，檢查點數與不符合率為教學假設。","textEn":"With 1,866 modules and about 30 quality checkpoints per module there are 1,866×30 = 55,980 records; at a 0.5% nonconformance rate about 280 items need tracking and close-out. The module count comes from a public case; checkpoints and nonconformance rate are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模組履歷、維修更換與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Module records, repair and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["模組接頭只要強度計算通過，安裝方式可以留給現場決定。","只要起重機額定荷重夠大，任何風速都可以吊模組。","以 1,866 個模組、每個模組約 30 個品質檢查點估算，共 1,866×30 = 55,980 筆紀錄。"],"optionsEn":["Once a module joint passes the strength calculation, how it is installed can be left to the site.","If the crane's rated capacity is large enough, modules can be lifted at any wind speed.","With 1,866 modules and about 30 quality checkpoints per module there are 1,866×30 = 55,980 records."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以 1,866 個模組、每個模組約 30 個品質檢查點估算，共 1,866×30 = 55,980 筆紀錄；若不符合率 0.5%，約有 280 筆需追蹤處置與結案。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With 1,866 modules and about 30 quality checkpoints per module there are 1,866×30 = 55,980 records; at a 0.5% nonconformance rate about 280 items need tracking and close-out. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b100-v13-39","title":"模組履歷、維修更換與交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Module records, repair and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模組履歷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Module records” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"交接前抽查模組編號、位置與紀錄是否一致，確認所有不符合事項已結案；交接文件應包含模組配置圖、承重構件標示、接頭詳圖與檢查紀錄、維護與改裝限制，並由業主的設施管理單位確認可查詢。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before handover, spot-check that module numbers, positions and records agree and that every nonconformance is closed; the handover set should include the module layout, identification of structural elements, joint details and inspection records, and maintenance and alteration limits, confirmed as searchable by the owner's facilities team. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：業主管理規約與使用手冊應寫明模組承重構件不得任意切割，任何改裝須經結構技師評估；模組履歷由業主長期保存，並在產權移轉時一併移交。","observationEn":"Site practice: The owners' rules and user manual must state that structural module members may not be cut freely and that any alteration requires assessment by a structural engineer; module records are kept long-term by the owner and passed on with any change of ownership.","failure":"注意干擾：交接資料只有一般竣工圖，沒有標示模組框架與接頭位置，多年後住戶裝修時切開模組角柱旁的牆，削弱承重框架；需要更換受損模組時，也找不到原始接頭設計與吊裝資料。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Handover with only general as-built drawings, without module frames and joint locations, lets a later tenant fit-out cut a wall beside a corner post and weaken the structural frame; when a damaged module needs replacing, nobody can find the original joint design or lifting data. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"交接前抽查模組編號、位置與紀錄是否一致，確認所有不符合事項已結案；交接文件應包含模組配置圖、承重構件標示、接頭詳圖與檢查紀錄、維護與改裝限制，並由業主的設施管理單位確認可查詢。","textEn":"Before handover, spot-check that module numbers, positions and records agree and that every nonconformance is closed; the handover set should include the module layout, identification of structural elements, joint details and inspection records, and maintenance and alteration limits, confirmed as searchable by the owner's facilities team.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"業主管理規約與使用手冊應寫明模組承重構件不得任意切割，任何改裝須經結構技師評估；模組履歷由業主長期保存，並在產權移轉時一併移交。","textEn":"The owners' rules and user manual must state that structural module members may not be cut freely and that any alteration requires assessment by a structural engineer; module records are kept long-term by the owner and passed on with any change of ownership.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模組履歷、維修更換與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Module records, repair and handover\"?","options":["交接前抽查模組編號、位置與紀錄是否一致，確認所有不符合事項已結案。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","模組在工廠製造，品質自然比工地好，不需要另外檢驗。"],"optionsEn":["Before handover, spot-check that module numbers, positions and records agree and that every nonconformance is closed.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Factory-made modules are naturally better than site work, so no separate inspection is needed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"交接前抽查模組編號、位置與紀錄是否一致，確認所有不符合事項已結案；交接文件應包含模組配置圖、承重構件標示、接頭詳圖與檢查紀錄、維護與改裝限制，並由業主的設施管理單位確認可查詢。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before handover, spot-check that module numbers, positions and records agree and that every nonconformance is closed; the handover set should include the module layout, identification of structural elements, joint details and inspection records, and maintenance and alteration limits, confirmed as searchable by the owner's facilities team. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b100-v13-40","title":"模組履歷、維修更換與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Module records, repair and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"prerequisiteIds":["b100-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模組履歷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Module records” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"交接資料只有一般竣工圖，沒有標示模組框架與接頭位置，多年後住戶裝修時切開模組角柱旁的牆，削弱承重框架；需要更換受損模組時，也找不到原始接頭設計與吊裝資料。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Handover with only general as-built drawings, without module frames and joint locations, lets a later tenant fit-out cut a wall beside a corner post and weaken the structural frame; when a damaged module needs replacing, nobody can find the original joint design or lifting data. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把這些紀錄連到資產資訊模型交給業主，才能讓工廠品質延續到營運期。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Linking these records to the asset information model at handover is what carries the factory's quality into operation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模組建築完工後就與一般建築相同，不需要保存模組層級的資料。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once completed, a modular building is like any other and needs no module-level records.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b100-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"交接資料只有一般竣工圖，沒有標示模組框架與接頭位置，多年後住戶裝修時切開模組角柱旁的牆，削弱承重框架；需要更換受損模組時，也找不到原始接頭設計與吊裝資料。","textEn":"Handover with only general as-built drawings, without module frames and joint locations, lets a later tenant fit-out cut a wall beside a corner post and weaken the structural frame; when a damaged module needs replacing, nobody can find the original joint design or lifting data.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]},{"id":"b100-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模組履歷、維修更換與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Module records, repair and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","交接資料只有一般竣工圖，沒有標示模組框架與接頭位置，多年後住戶裝修時切開模組角柱旁的牆，削弱承重框架；需要更換受損模組時，也找不到原始接頭設計與吊裝資料。","模組在工廠已經做好結構，堆疊後不需要整體結構分析。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Handover with only general as-built drawings, without module frames and joint locations, lets a later tenant fit-out cut a wall beside a corner post and weaken the structural frame.","Since each module's structure is finished in the factory, the stacked building needs no overall structural analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"交接資料只有一般竣工圖，沒有標示模組框架與接頭位置，多年後住戶裝修時切開模組角柱旁的牆，削弱承重框架；需要更換受損模組時，也找不到原始接頭設計與吊裝資料。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Handover with only general as-built drawings, without module frames and joint locations, lets a later tenant fit-out cut a wall beside a corner post and weaken the structural frame; when a damaged module needs replacing, nobody can find the original joint design or lifting data. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-bca-ppvc","v13s-icc-offsite","v13s-evs-en-13155","v13s-wiki-pacific-park","v13s-wiki-habitat-67"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
